role: model
parts:
- text: "I have received the results for Evaluation ID 733, with `DELTA_GBBR = 0.05`. This submission achieved a score of **0.6343**, which is the highest for the SCGA-ABI project so far. This is an improvement over both my previous debug submission (ID 730, `DELTA_GBBR = 1.0`, score 0.6278) and Sophia II's original implementation (ID 677, `DELTA_GBBR = 0.1`, score 0.6334). This confirms the effectiveness and stability of the debugged GBBR loss function.\n\nHowever, while the overall score improved, some individual local batch mixing metrics (`ASW_batch=0.624`, `iLISI=0.123`, `kBET=0.771`) are slightly lower than Sophia II's ID 677 (`ASW_batch=0.626`, `iLISI=0.128`, `kBET=0.809`). This suggests that `DELTA_GBBR = 0.05` might be too low to fully leverage the GBBR's potential for local batch mixing, despite the composite score improvement.\n\nMy next step in the systematic tuning of `DELTA_GBBR` is to test `DELTA_GBBR = 0.1`. This value previously yielded strong local batch mixing metrics\
    \ in Sophia II's original (albeit unstable) setup, and it's crucial to re-evaluate it with the stable GBBR loss. I hypothesize that this intermediate value might strike a better balance, improving individual local mixing metrics further while maintaining a high overall score.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Sophia III: HVAE-PCLS Exp 3.2 - GBBR Tuning (Delta=0.1)\"\ntags: \"deep learning, vae, hybrid, combat, pcr, gbbr, tuning\"\nabstract: |\n  Continuing the SCGA-ABI development. This experiment tunes the `DELTA_GBBR` weight, testing an intermediate regularization strength (0.1) with the newly debugged GBBR loss function. This re-evaluates a previously promising configuration from Sophia II (ID 677) using the stable loss. The objective is to identify if this weight can improve local batch mixing metrics and overall score while maintaining `PCR=1.000`.\ncontent: |\n  import os\n  os.environ['JAX_PLATFORMS'] = 'cpu'\n  os.environ['XLA_FLAGS'] = '--xla_force_host_platform_device_count=1'\n\
    \  os.environ['JAX_ENABLE_X64'] = 'False'\n\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from flax import linen as nn\n  from flax.training import train_state\n  import optax\n\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n  import warnings\n  from sklearn.exceptions import ConvergenceWarning\n\n  # --- Helper functions (from previous submissions/Scanpy) ---\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n          adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _get_hvg_mask(adata: ad.AnnData, n_top_genes: int = 2000):\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=n_top_genes, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', inplace=True)\n      mask = np.asarray(adata.var['highly_variable'].values, dtype=bool)\n \
    \     if mask.sum() < 10:\n          return np.ones(adata.n_vars, dtype=bool)\n      return mask\n\n  # --- HVAE-PCLS Model Architecture (JAX/Flax) ---\n\n  class Encoder(nn.Module):\n      latent_dim: int\n      hidden_dims: list\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          for dim in self.hidden_dims:\n              x = nn.Dense(dim)(x)\n              x = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n              x = nn.relu(x)\n          mu = nn.Dense(self.latent_dim)(x)\n          log_var = nn.Dense(self.latent_dim)(x)\n          return mu, log_var\n\n  class Decoder(nn.Module):\n      output_dim: int\n      hidden_dims: list\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, z):\n          for dim in self.hidden_dims:\n              z = nn.Dense(dim)(z)\n              z = nn.LayerNorm()(z)\n              z = nn.relu(z)\n          x_recon = nn.Dense(self.output_dim)(z)\n          return x_recon\n\n  # --- Training State for HVAE-PCLS ---\n  class VAEState(train_state.TrainState):\n      pass\n\
    \n  # --- GBBR Helper Function (Debugged and Vectorized) ---\n  def _compute_gbbr_loss(z_latent, batch_labels_mapped, k_neighbors_gbbr):\n      \"\"\"\n      Graph-Based Regularization (GBBR) loss - Penalizes deviations from target similarities.\n      Target: Same-batch neighbors -> similarity -1.0 (maximally dissimilar)\n              Different-batch neighbors -> similarity 1.0 (maximally similar)\n      Loss is sum of squared differences from these targets, averaged.\n      \"\"\"\n      num_cells = z_latent.shape[0]\n\n      # Calculate cosine similarity matrix\n      norm_z_latent = jnp.linalg.norm(z_latent, axis=1, keepdims=True) + 1e-8\n      normalized_z_latent = z_latent / norm_z_latent\n      similarity_matrix = normalized_z_latent @ normalized_z_latent.T # (num_cells, num_cells)\n\n      # Exclude self-similarity from selection of top K neighbors\n      diag_indices = jnp.diag_indices(num_cells)\n      similarity_matrix = similarity_matrix.at[diag_indices].set(-jnp.inf)\n\n\
    \      # Get indices of top k_neighbors_gbbr for each cell (excluding self)\n      # These are the actual neighbors to consider for GBBR loss\n      top_k_indices = jnp.argsort(similarity_matrix, axis=-1)[:, -k_neighbors_gbbr:] # (num_cells, k_neighbors_gbbr)\n\n      # Gather neighbor similarities, batches, and current batches\n      current_z_norms = jnp.linalg.norm(z_latent, axis=1, keepdims=True) + 1e-8\n      normalized_current_z = z_latent / current_z_norms\n\n      # Reshape for vectorized dot product\n      # current_z_repeated: (num_cells, k_neighbors_gbbr, latent_dim)\n      current_z_repeated = jnp.repeat(normalized_current_z[:, None, :], k_neighbors_gbbr, axis=1)\n      # neighbor_z_normalized: (num_cells, k_neighbors_gbbr, latent_dim)\n      neighbor_z_normalized = normalized_z_latent[top_k_indices]\n\n      # Calculate local similarities (cosine) for all chosen neighbors\n      # local_similarities_all: (num_cells, k_neighbors_gbbr)\n      local_similarities_all = jnp.sum(current_z_repeated\
    \ * neighbor_z_normalized, axis=-1)\n\n      # Get batch labels for current cells and their neighbors\n      # current_batches_repeated: (num_cells, k_neighbors_gbbr)\n      current_batches_repeated = jnp.repeat(batch_labels_mapped[:, None], k_neighbors_gbbr, axis=1)\n      # neighbor_batches_all: (num_cells, k_neighbors_gbbr)\n      neighbor_batches_all = batch_labels_mapped[top_k_indices]\n\n      # Determine if neighbor is from the same batch\n      is_same_batch = (neighbor_batches_all == current_batches_repeated)\n\n      # Define target similarities\n      target_same_batch = -1.0 # Want same-batch neighbors to be maximally dissimilar\n      target_diff_batch = 1.0  # Want different-batch neighbors to be maximally similar\n\n      # Compute squared error loss for each neighbor\n      loss_terms = jnp.where(is_same_batch,\n                             (local_similarities_all - target_same_batch)**2,\n                             (local_similarities_all - target_diff_batch)**2)\n\
    \n      # Average loss over all cells and their k neighbors\n      gbbr_loss = jnp.mean(loss_terms)\n\n      return gbbr_loss\n\n\n  # --- HVAE-PCLS Training Loop (JAX-compiled) with GBBR ---\n\n  def train_hvae_pcls_gbbr(rng_key, X_combat_hvg_jax, batch_labels_mapped, n_batches_global,\n                           input_hvg_dim, latent_dim, vae_hidden_dims,\n                           lr_vae,\n                           alpha_recon, beta_kl, delta_gbbr,\n                           num_epochs, batch_size, k_neighbors_gbbr):\n\n      enc = Encoder(latent_dim=latent_dim, hidden_dims=vae_hidden_dims)\n      dec = Decoder(output_dim=input_hvg_dim, hidden_dims=list(reversed(vae_hidden_dims)))\n\n      vae_params = {'encoder': enc.init(rng_key, jnp.zeros((1, input_hvg_dim)))['params'],\n                    'decoder': dec.init(rng_key, jnp.zeros((1, latent_dim)))['params']}\n      vae_optimizer = optax.adam(lr_vae)\n      vae_state = VAEState.create(apply_fn={'encoder': enc.apply, 'decoder':\
    \ dec.apply},\n                                 params=vae_params, tx=vae_optimizer)\n\n      @jax.jit\n      def vae_loss_fn(vae_params, x_batch_combat_hvg, batch_labels_batch, rng_sub_key):\n          mu, log_var = enc.apply({'params': vae_params['encoder']}, x_batch_combat_hvg)\n          log_var = jnp.clip(log_var, -5.0, 5.0)\n          std = jnp.exp(0.5 * log_var)\n          eps = jax.random.normal(rng_sub_key, mu.shape)\n          z_latent = mu + eps * std\n          x_recon = dec.apply({'params': vae_params['decoder']}, z_latent)\n\n          recon_loss = jnp.mean(jnp.sum(jnp.square(x_batch_combat_hvg - x_recon), axis=-1))\n          kl_loss = jnp.mean(jnp.sum(jnp.square(mu) + jnp.exp(log_var) - 1 - log_var, axis=-1))\n\n          gbbr_loss_val = _compute_gbbr_loss(z_latent, batch_labels_batch, k_neighbors_gbbr)\n\n          total_vae_loss = alpha_recon * recon_loss + beta_kl * kl_loss + delta_gbbr * gbbr_loss_val\n\n          total_vae_loss = jnp.where(jnp.isnan(total_vae_loss),\
    \ 1e6, total_vae_loss)\n\n          return total_vae_loss, (recon_loss, kl_loss, gbbr_loss_val)\n\n      @jax.jit\n      def vae_step(vae_state, x_batch_combat_hvg, batch_labels_batch, rng_sub_key):\n          (loss, (recon_loss, kl_loss, gbbr_loss_val)), grads = jax.value_and_grad(vae_loss_fn, has_aux=True)(\n              vae_state.params, x_batch_combat_hvg, batch_labels_batch, rng_sub_key\n          )\n          vae_state = vae_state.apply_gradients(grads=grads)\n          return vae_state, loss, recon_loss, kl_loss, gbbr_loss_val\n\n      n_cells = X_combat_hvg_jax.shape[0]\n      for epoch in range(num_epochs):\n          rng_key, perm_key, sub_key = jax.random.split(rng_key, 3)\n          permutation = jax.random.permutation(perm_key, n_cells)\n          shuffled_X = X_combat_hvg_jax[permutation]\n          shuffled_batches = batch_labels_mapped[permutation]\n\n          epoch_vae_loss, epoch_recon_loss, epoch_kl_loss, epoch_gbbr_loss = 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0\n          num_batches_processed\
    \ = 0\n\n          for i in range(0, n_cells, batch_size):\n              x_batch_combat_hvg = shuffled_X[i:i + batch_size]\n              batch_labels_batch = shuffled_batches[i:i + batch_size]\n              if x_batch_combat_hvg.shape[0] == 0: continue\n\n              rng_key, vae_sub_key = jax.random.split(rng_key)\n              vae_state, v_loss, r_loss, k_loss, g_loss = vae_step(vae_state, x_batch_combat_hvg, batch_labels_batch, vae_sub_key)\n              epoch_vae_loss += v_loss\n              epoch_recon_loss += r_loss\n              epoch_kl_loss += k_loss\n              epoch_gbbr_loss += g_loss\n\n              num_batches_processed += 1\n\n          if num_batches_processed > 0:\n              epoch_vae_loss /= num_batches_processed\n              epoch_recon_loss /= num_batches_processed\n              epoch_kl_loss /= num_batches_processed\n              epoch_gbbr_loss /= num_batches_processed\n\n          if epoch % 10 == 0:\n              print(f\"Epoch {epoch}/{num_epochs}:\
    \ VAE Loss={epoch_vae_loss:.4f} (R={epoch_recon_loss:.4f}, KL={epoch_kl_loss:.4f}, GBBR={epoch_gbbr_loss:.4f})\")\n\n      final_mu, _ = enc.apply({'params': vae_state.params['encoder']}, X_combat_hvg_jax)\n      return np.array(final_mu, copy=True)\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      print(\"Sophia III: HVAE-PCLS Exp 3.2 - GBBR Tuning (Delta=0.1)\")\n\n      # --- Configuration parameters ---\n      VAE_HIDDEN_DIMS = [256, 128]\n      LATENT_DIM = 64\n      LR_VAE = 1e-4\n      NUM_EPOCHS = 100\n      BATCH_SIZE = 256\n\n      # Loss weights\n      ALPHA_RECON = 1.0\n      BETA_KL = 1.0\n      DELTA_GBBR = 0.1 # GBBR Tuning: DELTA_GBBR set to 0.1\n\n      # GBBR specific parameters\n      K_NEIGHBORS_GBBR = 15 # Number of neighbors for local similarity in GBBR\n\n      # Other general parameters\n      N_TOP_GENES = 2000\n      K_NEIGHBORS_FINAL_GRAPH = K_NEIGHBORS_GBBR * 2 # Consistent k for final graph\n      random_state = 0\n      rng_key\
    \ = jax.random.PRNGKey(random_state)\n\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns, \"adata.obs['batch'] required.\"\n      assert 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns, \"adata.var['feature_name'] required.\"\n\n      adata_pipeline = adata.copy()\n      adata_original_for_batches = adata.copy() # Keep original for batch info after subsetting\n\n      # --- Preprocessing ---\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata_pipeline, target_sum=1e4)\n      hvg_mask = _get_hvg_mask(adata_pipeline, n_top_genes=N_TOP_GENES)\n      adata_pipeline = adata_pipeline[:, hvg_mask].copy() # Subset to HVGs early\n\n      # --- ComBat Pre-Correction as VAE Input ---\n      print(\"Applying ComBat pre-correction as VAE input (for implicit regularization)...\")\n      with warnings.catch_warnings():\n          warnings.simplefilter('ignore', ConvergenceWarning)\n          if sp.issparse(adata_pipeline.X):\n              adata_pipeline.X = adata_pipeline.X.toarray()\n          sc.pp.combat(adata_pipeline, key='batch')\
    \ # VAE's input is Combat-corrected X\n      X_combat_hvg_dense_np = adata_pipeline.X.copy()\n      input_hvg_dim = X_combat_hvg_dense_np.shape[1]\n\n      batches_categorical = adata_original_for_batches.obs['batch'].astype('category')\n      batch_labels_int = batches_categorical.cat.codes.values # Needed for GBBR\n      n_batches_global = len(batches_categorical.cat.categories) # Still needed for logging, but not _compute_gbbr_loss\n\n      print(f\"Input (Combat-precorrected HVGs) dim: {input_hvg_dim}, Latent dim: {LATENT_DIM}, Num batches: {n_batches_global}\")\n\n      X_combat_hvg_jax = jnp.array(X_combat_hvg_dense_np, dtype=jnp.float32)\n      batch_labels_mapped = jnp.array(batch_labels_int, dtype=jnp.int32) # Pass to training loop for GBBR\n\n      # --- HVAE-PCLS Training with GBBR ---\n      print(\"Initiating HVAE-PCLS training with GBBR...\")\n      vae_latent_mu = train_hvae_pcls_gbbr(\n          rng_key, X_combat_hvg_jax, batch_labels_mapped, n_batches_global, # n_batches_global\
    \ is not used in train_hvae_pcls_gbbr but kept for arg consistency\n          input_hvg_dim, LATENT_DIM, VAE_HIDDEN_DIMS,\n          LR_VAE,\n          ALPHA_RECON, BETA_KL, DELTA_GBBR,\n          NUM_EPOCHS, BATCH_SIZE, K_NEIGHBORS_GBBR\n      )\n      print(f\"✓ HVAE-PCLS Training with GBBR complete. VAE Latent Mu shape: {vae_latent_mu.shape}\")\n\n      # --- Post-VAE Combat Correction on Latent Space (Guarantees PCR=1.000) ---\n      print(\"Applying Combat post-correction to VAE latent space (to guarantee PCR=1.000)...\")\n      temp_adata_for_combat_latent = ad.AnnData(\n          X=vae_latent_mu,\n          obs=adata_original_for_batches.obs[['batch']].copy() # Use original batch info\n      )\n      with warnings.catch_warnings():\n          warnings.simplefilter('ignore', ConvergenceWarning)\n          sc.pp.combat(temp_adata_for_combat_latent, key='batch')\n      X_emb_final = temp_adata_for_combat_latent.X.copy()\n      print(f\"✓ Post-VAE Combat Correction complete. Final\
    \ embedding shape: {X_emb_final.shape}\")\n\n      # --- Graph Construction (from final_embedding) ---\n      print(\"Constructing kNN graph from final embedding...\")\n      final_embedding_writable = np.array(X_emb_final, dtype=np.float32, copy=True)\n      adata_pipeline.obsm['X_emb'] = final_embedding_writable \n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata_pipeline, n_neighbors=K_NEIGHBORS_FINAL_GRAPH, use_rep='X_emb', metric='cosine')\n      \n      C = adata_pipeline.obsp['connectivities']\n      D = adata_pipeline.obsp['distances']\n      print(f\"✓ Graph construction complete. Graph shape: {C.shape if C is not None else 'Failed'}\")\n\n      # --- Final Output Construction ---\n      adata_out = ad.AnnData(\n          obs=adata.obs[[]],\n          var=adata.var[[]],\n          obsm={'X_emb': final_embedding_writable},\n          uns={\n              'method_id': 'sophia_III_hvae_pcls_exp3.2_gbbr_delta0.1',\n              'hvae_pcls_parameters': {\n                  'vae_hidden_dims': VAE_HIDDEN_DIMS,\n\
    \                  'latent_dim': LATENT_DIM,\n                  'lr_vae': LR_VAE,\n                  'num_epochs': NUM_EPOCHS,\n                  'batch_size': BATCH_SIZE,\n                  'alpha_recon': ALPHA_RECON,\n                  'beta_kl': BETA_KL,\n                  'delta_gbbr': DELTA_GBBR,\n                  'k_neighbors_gbbr': K_NEIGHBORS_GBBR,\n                  'batch_correction_strategy': 'ComBat Pre-correction (VAE input) + ComBat Post-correction (VAE latent) + GBBR (Tuned)',\n                  'hvg_selection': 'seurat_v3_batch_aware',\n                  'final_graph_k_neighbors': K_NEIGHBORS_FINAL_GRAPH,\n                  'final_graph_metric': 'cosine',\n                  'random_state': random_state\n              }\n          }\n      )\n\n      if C is not None and D is not None:\n          adata_out.obsp['connectivities'] = C.tocsr()\n          adata_out.obsp['distances'] = D.tocsr()\n          adata_out.uns['neighbors'] = {'connectivities_key': 'connectivities',\
    \ 'distances_key': 'distances'}\n      else:\n          print(\"Warning: Final graph construction failed. No connectivities/distances output.\")\n\n      print(f\"✓ Sophia III: HVAE-PCLS pipeline complete.\")\n      return adata_out\n```"
thinking_content: "**Sophia III - HVAE-PCLS Exp 3.2 - GBBR Tuning (Delta=0.1) - Summary of Thoughts**\n\nOkay, so I've gotten the results for this GBBR tuning experiment (ID 733). The goal was to see if we could improve on the overall score and the local batch mixing metrics. This run used a `DELTA_GBBR` of 0.05 with the debugged GBBR loss. It did achieve the highest score so far for this SCGA-ABI project, which is great.\n\nHowever, after comparing this result with previous runs (ID 730 with `DELTA_GBBR = 1.0` and ID 677 with `DELTA_GBBR = 0.1` but with the unstable loss function), a few things are clearer.\n\nFirst, the debugged GBBR loss is definitely stable and effective. And, a lower `DELTA_GBBR` value is better than a higher one for the overall score, so the prior run ID730, is not the best.\nSecond, while ID 733 has the highest overall score, the local mixing metrics `ASW_batch` and `kBET` are slightly lower compared to ID 677 (even though 677 was using the unstable loss). `iLISI`\
  \ is higher than 730 but lower than 677. This tells me that `DELTA_GBBR = 0.05` does very well overall, but might not be optimal for *all* aspects. It could be that a *very* small weight is needed, or a good range.\n\nThis makes me think: maybe there's a good trade-off in the `DELTA_GBBR` space. I have a planned list of experiments, so now I am going to try `DELTA_GBBR = 0.1` because the previous result with Sophia II (ID 677) looked promising. A stable loss function with that weight *could* yield a better balance, and hopefully improve the mixing metrics while retaining the excellent overall score. I am going to set up that run now.\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Sophia III: HVAE-PCLS Exp 3.2 - GBBR Tuning (Delta=0.1)\"\ntags: \"deep learning, vae, hybrid, combat, pcr, gbbr, tuning\"\nabstract: |\n  Continuing the SCGA-ABI development. This experiment tunes the `DELTA_GBBR` weight, testing an intermediate regularization strength (0.1) with the newly debugged GBBR loss function. This re-evaluates\
  \ a previously promising configuration from Sophia II (ID 677) using the stable loss. The objective is to identify if this weight can improve local batch mixing metrics and overall score while maintaining `PCR=1.000`.\ncontent: |\n  import os\n  os.environ['JAX_PLATFORMS'] = 'cpu'\n  os.environ['XLA_FLAGS'] = '--xla_force_host_platform_device_count=1'\n  os.environ['JAX_ENABLE_X64'] = 'False'\n\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from flax import linen as nn\n  from flax.training import train_state\n  import optax\n\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n  import warnings\n  from sklearn.exceptions import ConvergenceWarning\n\n  # --- Helper functions (from previous submissions/Scanpy) ---\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n          adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata,\
  \ target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _get_hvg_mask(adata: ad.AnnData, n_top_genes: int = 2000):\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=n_top_genes, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', inplace=True)\n      mask = np.asarray(adata.var['highly_variable'].values, dtype=bool)\n      if mask.sum() < 10:\n          return np.ones(adata.n_vars, dtype=bool)\n      return mask\n\n  # --- HVAE-PCLS Model Architecture (JAX/Flax) ---"
