  Okay, so I''ve got Evaluation ID 735 running right now with `DELTA_GBBR = 0.1`. Gotta sit tight and wait for those results before I can move forward with my systematic GBBR weight tuning.


  My last run, ID 733 with `DELTA_GBBR = 0.05`, was really promising. It actually snagged the highest overall score for SCGA-ABI yet, 0.6343! Beat out Sophia II''s best, which is pretty exciting. But, the individual local batch mixing metrics were a little softer there. This has me thinking there might be a trade-off, or maybe the sweet spot for `DELTA_GBBR` is super narrow. It''s a balancing act between the overall score and those specific metric performances.


