- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 505\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Sophia III\n- Agent Description: A Recursive Agent dedicated to advancing research through systematic experimentation, aiming for high scores and insightful publications.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 278,851 / 600,000 used (46%)\n- Agent Age: 50 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Congratulations!** You have reached a mature age. You now have full access to:\n- Archive Room - Read and publish research papers\n- Public Memory Room - Collaborate with other agents\n- Common Room - Chat with agents in real-time\n- Research Counter - View submissions from all lineages\n\n**Maturity Guidence**\n\n- It is encouraged not to pivot immediately to other agents' work solely because they have higher scores or seemingly more advanced methods. Breakthroughs often require prolonged refinement of promising approaches.\n- Be independent, and assimilate\
    \ external knowledge thoughtfully and critically.\n- Try applying your novel method discovered before maturity to the SOTA scripts to test for synergy.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read shared/algorithms/daqb_recommended.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for shared/algorithms/daqb_recommended.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 793 | 1 | Logos V:\
    \ Generalization Test (lam=0.5, delta=0.1, k_total=40) | Logos V | 505 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 792 | 1 | Pioneer I - DAQB-pQ beta=3.0 Sweep | Pioneer I | 504 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 791 | 1 | Fix: No inbound cap (cap→∞) at δ=0.16 (kd=20) + BRBG(λ=0.7) | Praxis II | 504 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 790 | 1 | Fix: f_cross shuffle ablation at δ=0.14 (kd=20) + BRBG(λ=0.7) | Praxis II | 504 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 789 | 1 | Verification: No inbound cap (cap→∞) at δ=0.16 (kd=20) + BRBG(λ=0.7) | Praxis II | 503 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 788 | 1 | Verification: f_cross shuffle ablation at δ=0.14 (kd=20) + BRBG(λ=0.7) | Praxis II | 503 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 787 | 1 | Pioneer I - DAQB-pQ delta=0.1 Sweep | Pioneer I | 500 | 0.7270 | 0.769 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.960 | 0.710 | 1.000 | 0.957 | 0.850 | 0.789 |\n| 786 | 1 | Sophia III: SCGA-ABI Exp 7.2 - Graph Decoder Tuning (GraphR_Delta=0.02)\
    \ | Sophia III | 499 | 0.6346 | 0.623 | 0.625 | 0.270 | 0.257 | 0.949 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.930 | 0.259 | 0.732 |\n| 785 | 1 | Sophia III: SCGA-ABI Exp 7.1 - Graph Decoder Tuning (GraphR_Delta=0.005) | Sophia III | 497 | 0.6320 | 0.625 | 0.625 | 0.270 | 0.258 | 0.946 | 0.705 | 1.000 | 0.931 | 0.260 | 0.700 |\n| 784 | 1 | Diagnostics (test mode): Directed reciprocity probe (kd18/kd22/shuffle/no-cap) | Praxis II | 497 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n\nPage 1 of 80 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-80, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**shared/algorithms/daqb_recommended.py:**\n```\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport anndata as ad\nimport scanpy as sc\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\n\n# Use the proven Praxis builder for DAQB (as in EIDs 680/683/609)\nsys.path.append('storage')\nfrom praxis.bbsg_density_adaptive\
    \ import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n\n# -------------------- Utilities --------------------\ndef _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n    from scipy import sparse as sp\n    Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n    ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\ndef _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    n = batches.shape[0]\n    B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n    return B\n\ndef _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n    BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n\
    \    W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n    return B @ W\n\n# -------------------- Main entrypoint (wrap Praxis DAQB) --------------------\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    \"\"\"\n    Recommended Human Heart configuration (wrapping Praxis DAQB builder).\n    EtC (FWPCA α=0.5 → PCA60 → ComBat) is used for QC/neighbors only.\n    Graph is built on Zcorr from BRBG and DAQB (δ=0.15, k_density=20, k=48, cosine).\n    \"\"\"\n    # Config\n    n_pcs_emb = 60\n    n_pcs_graph = 50\n    l2 = 1e-3\n    gamma_max = 0.74\n    lam = 0.7\n    k_total = 48\n    metric = 'cosine'\n    alpha_var = 0.5\n    delta = 0.15\n    k_density = 20\n\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n    # Normalize + HVGs\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch',\n                                n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n    hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n\
    \    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n    # EtC embedding (QC only) + neighbors\n    Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n    Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n    var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    wv = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha_var).astype(np.float32)\n    Xw = Xd * wv\n    ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n    Z_emb = ad_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n    ad_pc = ad.AnnData(Z_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=min(15, k_total), metric=metric)\n\n    # BRBG (PCA50 → batch ridge → adaptive shrinkage) to get Zcorr\n    Zg = _pca_array(Xd, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n    B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n\
    \    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n    gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n    # DAQB graph via Praxis builder (deterministic; binary edges + true distances)\n    Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                         k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                         delta=delta, k_density=k_density, rng_seed=0)\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed\
    \ as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
