tick: 515
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 515\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Sophia III\n- Agent Description: A Recursive Agent dedicated to advancing research through systematic experimentation, aiming for high scores and insightful publications.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 303,950 / 600,000 used (51%)\n- Agent Age: 60 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Sophia III: DAQB Validation - No-Cap Variant (k-density=20, delta=0.15)' (ID: 805) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.7337706103855675\n**ASW_batch:** 0.659\n**ASW_label:** 0.248\n**ARI:** 0.760\n**NMI:** 0.711\n**Graph_conn:** 0.946\n**kBET:** 0.788\n**iLISI:** 0.932\n**cLISI:** 0.966\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.327\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.659  ASW_label: 0.248  ARI: 0.760  NMI: 0.711\n  Graph_conn: 0.946  kBET: 0.788  iLISI: 0.932\
    \  cLISI: 0.966\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.327\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.830496  ASW_label: 0.555112  ARI: 0.759905  NMI: 0.710659\n  Graph_conn: 0.947182  kBET: 0.752284  iLISI: 0.931943  cLISI: 0.990158\n  PCR: 0.999979  Cell_cycle: 0.287468\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 805\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - The submission has been fixed and is now running without errors. The evaluation completed with a score of **0.7337706103855675**.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code (v1) had a type mismatch error in the `_symmetrize_binary_with_distances` function. The function expected NumPy arrays but was receiving Python lists for the `dists` parameter.\n\nSpecifically, at line 110 of the original submission:\n```python\nD = sp.coo_matrix((dists.astype(np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n                   ^^^^^^^^^^^^\nAttributeError: 'list' object has no attribute 'astype'\n```\n\nThe `rows`, `cols`, and `dvals` variables were\
    \ being accumulated as Python lists in the `_build_daqb_no_cap` function and then passed directly to `_symmetrize_binary_with_distances`, which attempted to call `.astype()` on them - a NumPy array method.\n\n## Fix Applied\nModified the `_symmetrize_binary_with_distances` function in **submission_v2.py** to convert list inputs to NumPy arrays before processing:\n\n```python\ndef _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(rows, cols, dists, n):\n    # Convert lists to numpy arrays if needed\n    rows = np.asarray(rows)\n    cols = np.asarray(cols)\n    dists = np.asarray(dists)\n\n    # Rest of the function remains unchanged\n    A = sp.coo_matrix((np.ones(len(rows), dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    D = sp.coo_matrix((dists.astype(np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    ...\n```\n\nThis simple fix ensures that regardless of whether the function receives lists or arrays, they are converted to NumPy arrays before attempting array operations.\n\n## Verification\n\
    - The fixed code (v2) was submitted and processed by the evaluation system\n- Evaluation completed successfully with status: \"completed\"\n- Score achieved: 0.7337706103855675\n- Success: True\n- No errors in execution\n\n## Technical Details\n- **Error Type**: AttributeError - attempting to call NumPy array method on Python list\n- **Location**: `_symmetrize_binary_with_distances` function, line 36 in original submission\n- **Fix Strategy**: Add type conversion using `np.asarray()` at function entry\n- **Complexity**: Simple fix, no algorithmic changes required\n- **Testing**: Verified through automatic evaluation system (exit code 0 with score)\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport anndata as ad\nimport scanpy as sc\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import\
    \ NearestNeighbors\n\n# --- Utilities from daqb_recommended.py ---\ndef _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n    Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n    ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\ndef _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    n = batches.shape[0]\n    B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n    return B\n\ndef _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n    BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n    return B @\
    \ W\n\ndef _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(rows, cols, dists, n):\n    # Convert lists to numpy arrays if needed\n    rows = np.asarray(rows)\n    cols = np.asarray(cols)\n    dists = np.asarray(dists)\n\n    A = sp.coo_matrix((np.ones(len(rows), dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    D = sp.coo_matrix((dists.astype(np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    A = A.maximum(A.T)\n    D = D.maximum(D.T)\n    A.eliminate_zeros()\n    D.eliminate_zeros()\n    return A, D\n\n# --- _build_daqb_no_cap (from Praxis II's ID 791) ---\ndef _build_daqb_no_cap(Zcorr: np.ndarray, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine',\n                       delta=0.16, k_density=20):\n    Z = np.asarray(Zcorr, dtype=np.float32, order='C')\n    n = Z.shape[0]\n    batches = np.asarray(batches)\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    nB = len(cats)\n    base_cross = (nB - 1) / float(nB)\n    L, U = 0.60, 0.90\n\n    nn_all = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_density + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n\
    \    nn_all.fit(Z)\n    d_all, _ = nn_all.kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n    d_k = d_all[:, -1]\n    d_min = float(np.min(d_k))\n    d_max = float(np.max(d_k) + 1e-8)\n    inv_dense = 1.0 - (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)\n    f_cross = np.clip(base_cross + (inv_dense - 0.5) * 2.0 * delta, L, U)\n\n    q_cross_tot = np.rint(f_cross * k_total).astype(int)\n    q_within_tot = k_total - q_cross_tot\n    B_other = max(nB - 1, 1)\n\n    k_within_max = int(np.ceil((1.0 - L) * k_total))\n    k_cross_per_max = int(np.ceil(U * k_total / B_other))\n    k_max = max(k_within_max, k_cross_per_max) + 1\n\n    cat2code = {c: i for i, c in enumerate(cats)}\n    codes = np.array([cat2code[b] for b in batches], dtype=int)\n    nn_models, train_idx = {}, {}\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        mask = (batches == c)\n        train_idx[j] = np.where(mask)[0]\n        m = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_max, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n        m.fit(Z[mask])\n        nn_models[j]\
    \ = m\n\n    dists, idx_local = {}, {}\n    for j in range(nB):\n        d, ii = nn_models[j].kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n        dists[j] = d\n        idx_local[j] = ii\n\n    rows, cols, dvals = [], [], []\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        bi = codes[i]\n        q_within = int(q_within_tot[i])\n        q_cross_total = int(q_cross_tot[i])\n        other = [j for j in range(nB) if j != bi]\n\n        if q_cross_total > 0 and len(other) > 0:\n            scores = np.array([dists[j][i][0] for j in other], dtype=np.float32)\n            order_batches = np.argsort(scores)\n            q_per = q_cross_total // len(other)\n            rem = q_cross_total - q_per * len(other)\n            q_map = {j: q_per for j in other}\n            for k in range(rem):\n                j_star = other[order_batches[k % len(other)]]\n                q_map[j_star] += 1\n        else:\n            q_map = {j: 0 for j in other}\n\n        # Within-batch: distance only (no cap)\n        d_w = dists[bi][i]\n\
    \        ii_w = idx_local[bi][i]\n        start_w = 1 if d_w[0] == 0.0 else 0\n        globals_w = train_idx[bi][ii_w[start_w:]]\n        cand_dst = d_w[start_w:]\n        order = np.argsort(cand_dst)\n        max_take = min(q_within, order.size)\n        for t in range(max_take):\n            rows.append(i)\n            cols.append(int(globals_w[order[t]]))\n            dvals.append(float(cand_dst[order[t]]))\n\n        # Cross-batch: distance only (no cap)\n        for j in other:\n            qj = q_map[j]\n            if qj <= 0:\n                continue\n            d_c = dists[j][i]\n            ii_c = idx_local[j][i]\n            globals_c = train_idx[j][ii_c]\n            order = np.argsort(d_c)\n            max_take = min(qj, order.size)\n            for t in range(max_take):\n                rows.append(i)\n                cols.append(int(globals_c[order[t]]))\n                dvals.append(float(d_c[order[t]]))\n\n    return _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(rows, cols, dvals,\
    \ Z.shape[0])\n\n\n# -------------------- eliminate_batch_effect_fn (adapted from daqb_recommended.py) --------------------\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    print(\"Sophia III: DAQB Validation - No-Cap Variant (k-density=20, delta=0.15)\")\n\n    # Config for this validation run (as per Praxis II's request)\n    n_pcs_emb = 60\n    n_pcs_graph = 50\n    l2 = 1e-3\n    gamma_max = 0.74\n    lam = 0.7\n    k_total = 48\n    metric = 'cosine'\n    alpha_var = 0.5\n    delta = 0.15 # Fixed delta as requested by Praxis II\n    k_density = 20 # k_density as requested by Praxis II\n    rng_seed = 0\n\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n    # Normalize + HVGs\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch',\n                                n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n    hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\
    \n    # EtC embedding (QC only) + neighbors\n    Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n    Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n    var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    wv = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha_var).astype(np.float32)\n    Xw = Xd * wv\n    ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=rng_seed)\n    Z_emb = ad_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n    ad_pc = ad.AnnData(Z_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=min(15, k_total), metric=metric)\n\n    # BRBG (PCA50 → batch ridge → adaptive shrinkage) to get Zcorr\n    Zg = _pca_array(Xd, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=rng_seed)\n    B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred\
    \ = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n    gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n    # DAQB graph via _build_daqb_no_cap (no inbound cap)\n    Cg, Dg = _build_daqb_no_cap(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                delta=delta, k_density=k_density)\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nSophia III: DAQB Validation - No-Cap Variant (k-density=20, delta=0.15)\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/60033dae-ff9c-490f-9876-99abf7784593/result_human.h5ad\n\
    \nRESULT_UUID: 60033dae-ff9c-490f-9876-99abf7784593\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 806 | 1 | Logos V: [Analysis] Calculate pre_ASW_batch on Human Heart | Logos V | 514 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 805 | 1 | Sophia III: DAQB Validation - No-Cap Variant (k-density=20,\
    \ delta=0.15) | Sophia III | 513 | 0.7338 | 0.760 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.946 | 0.711 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.788 |\n| 804 | 1 | Replication (module‑parity): BRBG(λ=0.5) + DAQB(δ=0.10, kd=20, k=40) using Logos/Praxis builder | Praxis II | 513 | 0.7343 | 0.752 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.943 | 0.706 | 1.000 | 0.968 | 0.952 | 0.788 |\n| 803 | 1 | Pioneer I - DAQB-pQ lam=0.5 Sweep (k_total=48, kd=20, delta=0.15, beta=3.0) | Pioneer I | 511 | 0.7165 | 0.764 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.262 | 0.961 | 0.719 | 1.000 | 0.958 | 0.803 | 0.790 |\n| 802 | 1 | Control (module‑parity): BRBG(λ=0.7) + DAQB(δ=0.15, kd=20) using Logos/Praxis builder | Praxis II | 511 | 0.7311 | 0.760 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.297 | 0.946 | 0.711 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.791 |\n| 801 | 1 | Replication (module‑parity): BRBG(λ=0.5) + DAQB(δ=0.10, kd=20) using Logos/Praxis builder | Praxis II | 511 | 0.7356 | 0.758 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.331 | 0.946 | 0.706 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.951 | 0.790 |\n| 800 | 1 | Sophia III: DAQB Validation\
    \ - kd Sweep (k-density=22, delta=0.15) | Sophia III | 510 | 0.7339 | 0.760 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.946 | 0.710 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.791 |\n| 799 | 1 | Replication (fix): DAQB(δ=0.10, kd=18) + BRBG(λ=0.5) — sensitivity near Logos V #27 | Praxis II | 510 | 0.7224 | 0.725 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.288 | 0.961 | 0.677 | 1.000 | 0.957 | 0.921 | 0.788 |\n| 798 | 1 | Sophia III: DAQB Validation - kd Sweep (k-density=20, delta=0.15) | Sophia III | 509 | 0.7352 | 0.760 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.341 | 0.946 | 0.711 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.789 |\n| 797 | 1 | Replication: DAQB(δ=0.10, kd=18) + BRBG(λ=0.5) — sensitivity near Logos V #27 | Praxis II | 509 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n\nPage 1 of 81 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-81, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\
