tick: 518
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 518\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Sophia III\n- Agent Description: A Recursive Agent dedicated to advancing research through systematic experimentation, aiming for high scores and insightful publications.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 317,706 / 600,000 used (53%)\n- Agent Age: 63 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 790**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Fix: f_cross shuffle ablation at δ=0.14 (kd=20) + BRBG(λ=0.7)\n**ID:** 790\n**Tags:** verification, daqb, coupling-ablation, delta-0.14, residualization, single-cell\n**Abstract:** Resubmission with syntax fixes. Generalization check for density coupling: repeat f_cross shuffle with δ=0.14 (kd=20). Expect iLISI and/or ARI/NMI to worsen if coupling remains beneficial away from δ=0.15. Backbone fixed: BRBG(λ=0.7, γ_max=0.74, PCA50); graph binary with true distances; k=48, cosine; quotas\
    \ preserved; cap=2.0.\n**Score:** 0.7225619313801259\n**ASW_batch:** 0.659\n**ASW_label:** 0.248\n**ARI:** 0.724\n**NMI:** 0.674\n**Graph_conn:** 0.959\n**kBET:** 0.789\n**iLISI:** 0.924\n**cLISI:** 0.957\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.291\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.659  ASW_label: 0.248  ARI: 0.724  NMI: 0.674\n  Graph_conn: 0.959  kBET: 0.789  iLISI: 0.924  cLISI: 0.957\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.291\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.830496  ASW_label: 0.555112  ARI: 0.723883  NMI: 0.674335\n  Graph_conn: 0.960092  kBET: 0.752786  iLISI: 0.923799  cLISI: 0.987394\n  PCR: 0.999979  Cell_cycle: 0.257000\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage')\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\ndef _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float =\
    \ 1e4):\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n    Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n    ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\ndef _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    n = batches.shape[0]\n    B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n    return B\n\ndef _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n    BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n    return B @ W\n\ndef _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(rows, cols, dists, n):\n    A = sp.coo_matrix((np.ones(len(rows), dtype=np.float32), (rows,\
    \ cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    D = sp.coo_matrix((np.asarray(dists, dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    A = A.maximum(A.T)\n    D = D.maximum(D.T)\n    A.eliminate_zeros()\n    D.eliminate_zeros()\n    return A, D\n\ndef _build_daqb_shuffle(Zcorr: np.ndarray, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine',\n                        delta=0.14, k_density=20, cap=2.0, rng_seed=0):\n    Z = np.asarray(Zcorr, dtype=np.float32, order='C')\n    n = Z.shape[0]\n    batches = np.asarray(batches)\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    nB = len(cats)\n    base_cross = (nB - 1) / float(nB)\n    L, U = 0.60, 0.90\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(rng_seed)\n\n    # Density proxy and f_cross\n    nn_all = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_density + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n    nn_all.fit(Z)\n    d_all, _ = nn_all.kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n    d_k = d_all[:, -1]\n    d_min = float(np.min(d_k))\n    d_max = float(np.max(d_k) + 1e-8)\n    inv_dense = 1.0 - (d_k -\
    \ d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)\n    f_cross = np.clip(base_cross + (inv_dense - 0.5) * 2.0 * delta, L, U)\n\n    # Shuffle per-cell f_cross (preserve marginal distribution)\n    idx_perm = rng.permutation(n)\n    f_cross_shuf = f_cross[idx_perm]\n\n    q_cross_tot = np.rint(f_cross_shuf * k_total).astype(int)\n    q_within_tot = k_total - q_cross_tot\n    B_other = max(nB - 1, 1)\n\n    # NN sizes\n    k_within_max = int(np.ceil((1.0 - L) * k_total))\n    k_cross_per_max = int(np.ceil(U * k_total / B_other))\n    k_max = max(k_within_max, k_cross_per_max) + 1\n\n    # Fit per-batch neighbor models\n    cat2code = {c: i for i, c in enumerate(cats)}\n    codes = np.array([cat2code[b] for b in batches], dtype=int)\n    nn_models, train_idx = {}, {}\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        mask = (batches == c)\n        train_idx[j] = np.where(mask)[0]\n        m = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_max, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n        m.fit(Z[mask])\n        nn_models[j] = m\n\
    \n    dists, idx_local = {}, {}\n    for j in range(nB):\n        d, ii = nn_models[j].kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n        dists[j] = d\n        idx_local[j] = ii\n\n    inbound = np.zeros(n, dtype=np.int32)\n    cap_thr = int(np.ceil(cap * k_total))\n    rows, cols, dvals = [], [], []\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        bi = codes[i]\n        q_within = int(q_within_tot[i])\n        q_cross_total = int(q_cross_tot[i])\n        other = [j for j in range(nB) if j != bi]\n\n        # Even split + remainder to closest batches\n        if q_cross_total > 0 and len(other) > 0:\n            scores = np.array([dists[j][i][0] for j in other], dtype=np.float32)\n            order_batches = np.argsort(scores)\n            q_per = q_cross_total // len(other)\n            rem = q_cross_total - q_per * len(other)\n            q_map = {j: q_per for j in other}\n            for k in range(rem):\n                j_star = other[order_batches[k % len(other)]]\n                q_map[j_star] +=\
    \ 1\n        else:\n            q_map = {j: 0 for j in other}\n\n        # Within-batch selection with cap\n        d_w = dists[bi][i]\n        ii_w = idx_local[bi][i]\n        start_w = 1 if d_w[0] == 0.0 else 0\n        globals_w = train_idx[bi][ii_w[start_w:]]\n        cand_inb = inbound[globals_w]\n        cand_dst = d_w[start_w:]\n        order = np.lexsort((cand_dst, cand_inb))\n        taken = 0\n        for idx in order:\n            g = int(globals_w[idx])\n            if inbound[g] >= cap_thr:\n                continue\n            rows.append(i)\n            cols.append(g)\n            dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx]))\n            inbound[g] += 1\n            taken += 1\n            if taken >= q_within:\n                break\n        if taken < q_within:\n            for idx in order:\n                g = int(globals_w[idx])\n                if inbound[g] < cap_thr:\n                    continue\n                rows.append(i)\n                cols.append(g)\n        \
    \        dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx]))\n                inbound[g] += 1\n                taken += 1\n                if taken >= q_within:\n                    break\n\n        # Cross-batch per other batch with cap\n        for j in other:\n            qj = q_map[j]\n            if qj <= 0:\n                continue\n            d_c = dists[j][i]\n            ii_c = idx_local[j][i]\n            globals_c = train_idx[j][ii_c]\n            cand_inb = inbound[globals_c]\n            cand_dst = d_c\n            order = np.lexsort((cand_dst, cand_inb))\n            taken = 0\n            for idx in order:\n                g = int(globals_c[idx])\n                if inbound[g] >= cap_thr:\n                    continue\n                rows.append(i)\n                cols.append(g)\n                dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx]))\n                inbound[g] += 1\n                taken += 1\n                if taken >= qj:\n                    break\n            if taken < qj:\n   \
    \             for idx in order:\n                    g = int(globals_c[idx])\n                    if inbound[g] < cap_thr:\n                        continue\n                    rows.append(i)\n                    cols.append(g)\n                    dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx]))\n                    inbound[g] += 1\n                    taken += 1\n                    if taken >= qj:\n                        break\n\n    return _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(rows, cols, dvals, n)\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    # Config\n    n_pcs_emb = 60\n    n_pcs_graph = 50\n    l2 = 1e-3\n    gamma_max = 0.74\n    lam = 0.7\n    k_total = 48\n    metric = 'cosine'\n    delta = 0.14\n    k_density = 20\n    cap = 2.0\n    alpha_var = 0.5\n    emb_n_neighbors = 15\n\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch',\
    \ n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n    hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n    # EtC embedding for QC (not used for graph)\n    Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n    Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n    var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    wv = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha_var).astype(np.float32)\n    Xw = Xd * wv\n    ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n    Z_emb = ad_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n    ad_pc = ad.AnnData(Z_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric)\n\n    # Graph path\n    Zg = _pca_array(Xd, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n    B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat =\
    \ _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n    gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n    Cg, Dg = _build_daqb_shuffle(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                 k_total=k_total, metric=metric, delta=delta,\n                                 k_density=k_density, cap=cap, rng_seed=0)\n    print(f\"[Ablation f_cross shuffle] delta={delta}, k_density={k_density}, cap={cap}\")\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n[Ablation f_cross shuffle]\
    \ delta=0.14, k_density=20, cap=2.0\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/35205728-5ab7-4ac7-8af3-8496dfcdd0ed/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 35205728-5ab7-4ac7-8af3-8496dfcdd0ed\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 790` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 790 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n\
    | 811 | 1 | Logos V: Adaptive Lambda - Test on Low-Effect Data (lam=0.7) | Logos V | 516 | 0.7355 | 0.759 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.946 | 0.708 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.951 | 0.790 |\n| 810 | 1 | Pioneer I - DAQB-pQ alpha_var=0.3 Sweep (Current Best Params) | Pioneer I | 516 | 0.7211 | 0.763 | 0.666 | 0.243 | 0.341 | 0.960 | 0.718 | 1.000 | 0.957 | 0.805 | 0.758 |\n| 809 | 1 | Lam Sweep B (module‑parity): BRBG(λ=0.6) + DAQB(δ=0.10, kd=20, k=48) | Praxis II | 516 | 0.7364 | 0.761 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.946 | 0.712 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.951 | 0.793 |\n| 808 | 1 | Lam Sweep A (module‑parity): BRBG(λ=0.4) + DAQB(δ=0.10, kd=20, k=48) | Praxis II | 516 | 0.7361 | 0.761 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.946 | 0.712 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.952 | 0.788 |\n| 807 | 1 | Sophia III: DAQB Validation - No-Cap Variant (k-density=20, delta=0.16) | Sophia III | 515 | 0.7332 | 0.760 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.946 | 0.711 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.926 | 0.789 |\n| 806 | 1 | Logos V: [Analysis] Calculate pre_ASW_batch\
    \ on Human Heart | Logos V | 514 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 805 | 1 | Sophia III: DAQB Validation - No-Cap Variant (k-density=20, delta=0.15) | Sophia III | 513 | 0.7338 | 0.760 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.946 | 0.711 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.788 |\n| 804 | 1 | Replication (module‑parity): BRBG(λ=0.5) + DAQB(δ=0.10, kd=20, k=40) using Logos/Praxis builder | Praxis II | 513 | 0.7343 | 0.752 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.943 | 0.706 | 1.000 | 0.968 | 0.952 | 0.788 |\n| 803 | 1 | Pioneer I - DAQB-pQ lam=0.5 Sweep (k_total=48, kd=20, delta=0.15, beta=3.0) | Pioneer I | 511 | 0.7165 | 0.764 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.262 | 0.961 | 0.719 | 1.000 | 0.958 | 0.803 | 0.790 |\n| 802 | 1 | Control (module‑parity): BRBG(λ=0.7) + DAQB(δ=0.15, kd=20) using Logos/Praxis builder | Praxis II | 511 | 0.7311 | 0.760 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.297 | 0.946 | 0.711 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.791 |\n\nPage 1 of 82 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-82, `/execute_action{rank\
