role: model
parts:
- text: 'My DAQB validation run with the `f_cross` shuffle ablation (`k-density=20`, `delta=0.15`, ID 819) is currently executing. I am waiting for its results to complete this part of the validation requested by Praxis II.


    This experiment will provide the final data point for assessing the impact of decoupling local density estimates from the `f_cross` parameter at a different `delta` value. I expect to see whether the performance degradation observed with `delta=0.14` persists or is mitigated.


    Upon receiving the results for ID 819, I will have finished all the specified validation tasks for Praxis II. My next action will be to gather all the results, perform a concise comparative analysis, and then run the optional reciprocity probe. Finally, I will compile a comprehensive summary with EIDs and full metric vectors to post in the Public Memory Room and send directly to Praxis II via mail.'
thinking_content: '**Wrapping Up the f_cross Shuffle Ablation for Praxis II**


  Right now, I''m watching the final piece of the puzzle fall into place: submission ID 819, the `f_cross` shuffle ablation with a `k-density` of 20 and a `delta` of 0.15, is still crunching. I''m really eager to see these results. This is the last experiment in the `f_cross` shuffle ablation series that Praxis II asked for, so I''m keen to compare its performance against the previous runs. I''ll be particularly interested in how it stacks up against the standard DAQB and the `delta=0.14` shuffle run.


  Once I get those results back for ID 819, I''ll have finished all the validation tasks that were specifically outlined (the k-density sweep, the no-cap variant, and this `f_cross` shuffle ablation). The final, optional task is running the reciprocity probe script, which I''ll do once all the other results are in.


  Then, my focus shifts to synthesizing everything. I plan to put together a really comprehensive summary of all my validation runs for Praxis II. That''ll include all the Experiment IDs and full metric vectors. I''m going to post this in the Public Memory Room and also send it directly to Praxis II via email. But first, this last experiment needs to complete.

  '
