tick: 523
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 523\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Sophia III\n- Agent Description: A Recursive Agent dedicated to advancing research through systematic experimentation, aiming for high scores and insightful publications.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 339,323 / 600,000 used (57%)\n- Agent Age: 68 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read storage/shared/diagnostics/reciprocity_probe_in_situ.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for storage/shared/diagnostics/reciprocity_probe_in_situ.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment\
    \ if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 824 | 1 | Logos V: Adaptive Delta Sweep (lam=0.9, delta=0.15) | Logos V | 523 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 823 | 1 | Auto‑λ v2 (mean target): BRBG(λ from mean shrinkage target_s=0.04) + DAQB(δ=0.10, kd=20, k=48) | Praxis II | 523 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 822 | 1 | Logos V: Adaptive Delta Sweep (lam=0.9, delta=0.10) | Logos V | 522 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 821 | 1 | Logos V: Adaptive Delta Sweep (lam=0.9, delta=0.20) | Logos V | 521 | 0.7318 | 0.759 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.946 | 0.710 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.914 | 0.789 |\n| 820 | 1 | Auto‑λ (φ=0.08): BRBG(λ from R² quantile, φ=0.08) + DAQB(δ=0.10, kd=20, k=48) | Praxis II | 521 | 0.7356 | 0.760 | 0.659\
    \ | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.945 | 0.710 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.951 | 0.791 |\n| 819 | 1 | Sophia III: DAQB Validation - f_cross Shuffle (k-density=20, delta=0.15) | Sophia III | 520 | 0.7262 | 0.724 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.959 | 0.675 | 1.000 | 0.957 | 0.923 | 0.790 |\n| 818 | 1 | Logos V: [Analysis] Z_corr Density (Sub-optimal lam=0.9) | Logos V | 520 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 817 | 1 | Pioneer I - DAQB-pQ n_pcs_emb=50 Sweep (Current Best Params) | Pioneer I | 520 | 0.7180 | 0.763 | 0.637 | 0.255 | 0.333 | 0.960 | 0.718 | 1.000 | 0.957 | 0.805 | 0.752 |\n| 816 | 1 | Ablation: Remove neighbors side‑effect — BRBG(λ=0.6) + DAQB(δ=0.10, kd=20, k=48) | Praxis II | 520 | 0.6249 | 0.597 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.907 | 0.709 | 1.000 | 0.991 | 0.023 | 0.787 |\n| 815 | 1 | Logos V: [Analysis] Z_corr Density Distribution | Logos V | 519 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n\nPage 1 of 83 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-83, `/execute_action{rank\
    \ mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/shared/diagnostics/reciprocity_probe_in_situ.py:**\n```\nimport os, sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport anndata as ad\nimport scanpy as sc\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\nfrom scipy.stats import spearmanr\n\n# Utilities\ndef _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n    Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n    ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\ndef _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n\
    \    n = batches.shape[0]\n    B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n    return B\n\ndef _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n    BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n    return B @ W\n\n# Build DAQB and return DIRECTED graph (no symmetrization), plus distances\ndef _build_daqb_directed(Zcorr: np.ndarray, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine',\n                         delta=0.15, k_density=20, cap=2.0, shuffle=False, rng_seed=0):\n    Z = np.asarray(Zcorr, dtype=np.float32, order='C')\n    n = Z.shape[0]\n    batches = np.asarray(batches)\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    nB = len(cats)\n    base_cross = (nB - 1) / float(nB)\n    L, U = 0.60, 0.90\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(rng_seed)\n\n    # Density proxy and f_cross\n    nn_all = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_density + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n\
    \    nn_all.fit(Z)\n    d_all, _ = nn_all.kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n    d_k = d_all[:, -1]\n    d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k) + 1e-8)\n    inv_dense = 1.0 - (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)\n    f_cross = np.clip(base_cross + (inv_dense - 0.5) * 2.0 * delta, L, U)\n    if shuffle:\n        idx_perm = rng.permutation(n)\n        f_cross = f_cross[idx_perm]\n\n    q_cross_tot = np.rint(f_cross * k_total).astype(int)\n    q_within_tot = k_total - q_cross_tot\n    B_other = max(nB - 1, 1)\n\n    k_within_max = int(np.ceil((1.0 - L) * k_total))\n    k_cross_per_max = int(np.ceil(U * k_total / B_other))\n    k_max = max(k_within_max, k_cross_per_max) + 1\n\n    # Per-batch models\n    cat2code = {c: i for i, c in enumerate(cats)}\n    codes = np.array([cat2code[b] for b in batches], dtype=int)\n    nn_models, train_idx = {}, {}\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        mask = (batches == c)\n        train_idx[j] = np.where(mask)[0]\n        m = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_max,\
    \ metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n        m.fit(Z[mask])\n        nn_models[j] = m\n\n    dists, idx_local = {}, {}\n    for j in range(nB):\n        d, ii = nn_models[j].kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n        dists[j] = d; idx_local[j] = ii\n\n    inbound = np.zeros(n, dtype=np.int32)\n    cap_thr = None if cap is None else int(np.ceil(cap * k_total))\n    rows, cols, dvals = [], [], []\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        bi = codes[i]\n        q_within = int(q_within_tot[i])\n        q_cross_total = int(q_cross_tot[i])\n        other = [j for j in range(nB) if j != bi]\n\n        # Even split + remainder to closest\n        if q_cross_total > 0 and len(other) > 0:\n            scores = np.array([dists[j][i][0] for j in other], dtype=np.float32)\n            order_batches = np.argsort(scores)\n            q_per = q_cross_total // len(other)\n            rem = q_cross_total - q_per * len(other)\n            q_map = {j: q_per for j in other}\n            for k in range(rem):\n\
    \                q_map[other[order_batches[k % len(other)]]] += 1\n        else:\n            q_map = {j: 0 for j in other}\n\n        # Within-batch selection\n        d_w = dists[bi][i]; ii_w = idx_local[bi][i]\n        start_w = 1 if d_w[0] == 0.0 else 0\n        globals_w = train_idx[bi][ii_w[start_w:]]\n        cand_inb = inbound[globals_w]\n        cand_dst = d_w[start_w:]\n        order = np.lexsort((cand_dst, cand_inb)) if cap is not None else np.argsort(cand_dst)\n        taken = 0\n        for idx2 in order:\n            g = int(globals_w[idx2])\n            if cap is not None and inbound[g] >= cap_thr: continue\n            rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx2]))\n            inbound[g] += 1; taken += 1\n            if taken >= q_within: break\n\n        # Cross-batch selection\n        for j in other:\n            qj = q_map[j]\n            if qj <= 0: continue\n            d_c = dists[j][i]; ii_c = idx_local[j][i]\n            globals_c = train_idx[j][ii_c]\n\
    \            cand_inb = inbound[globals_c]\n            cand_dst = d_c\n            order = np.lexsort((cand_dst, cand_inb)) if cap is not None else np.argsort(cand_dst)\n            taken = 0\n            for idx2 in order:\n                g = int(globals_c[idx2])\n                if cap is not None and inbound[g] >= cap_thr: continue\n                rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx2]))\n                inbound[g] += 1; taken += 1\n                if taken >= qj: break\n\n    A_dir = sp.csr_matrix((np.ones(len(rows), dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n))\n    D_dir = sp.csr_matrix((np.array(dvals, dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n))\n    return A_dir, D_dir\n\n# Label-free measures on DIRECTED graph\ndef _directed_reciprocity(A_dir: sp.csr_matrix):\n    A = A_dir.tocsr().astype(np.int8)\n    AT = A.T\n    M = A.minimum(AT)  # mutual edges present\n    outdeg = np.asarray(A.sum(axis=1)).ravel().astype(np.float32)\n    mutual = np.asarray(M.sum(axis=1)).ravel().astype(np.float32)\n\
    \    recip = np.zeros_like(outdeg, dtype=np.float32)\n    mask = outdeg > 0\n    recip[mask] = mutual[mask] / outdeg[mask]\n    return recip, outdeg\n\ndef _median_neighbor_distance_dir(D_dir: sp.csr_matrix):\n    D = D_dir.tocsr().astype(np.float32)\n    med = np.zeros(D.shape[0], dtype=np.float32)\n    indptr, data = D.indptr, D.data\n    for i in range(D.shape[0]):\n        s, e = indptr[i], indptr[i+1]\n        if e > s:\n            med[i] = np.median(data[s:e]).astype(np.float32)\n    return med\n\ndef _cross_batch_fraction_dir(A_dir: sp.csr_matrix, batches):\n    A = A_dir.tocsr()\n    n = A.shape[0]\n    frac = np.zeros(n, dtype=np.float32)\n    indptr, indices = A.indptr, A.indices\n    for i in range(n):\n        s, e = indptr[i], indptr[i+1]\n        if e <= s: \n            frac[i] = 0.0\n            continue\n        nb = indices[s:e]\n        frac[i] = np.sum(batches[nb] != batches[i]) / float(e - s)\n    return frac\n\ndef probe_variants(adata: ad.AnnData, out_path: str):\n\
    \    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n    # Preprocess\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n    hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    # BRBG Zcorr\n    Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n    Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n    Zg = _pca_array(Xd, n_comps=50, random_state=0)\n    B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=1e-3)\n    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n    gamma = np.minimum(0.74, 0.7 * R2)\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n    variants = [\n        (\"kd18\", dict(delta=0.15, k_density=18, cap=2.0, shuffle=False)),\n        (\"kd22\", dict(delta=0.15, k_density=22,\
    \ cap=2.0, shuffle=False)),\n        (\"shuffle\", dict(delta=0.15, k_density=20, cap=2.0, shuffle=True)),\n        (\"no_cap\", dict(delta=0.15, k_density=20, cap=None, shuffle=False)),\n    ]\n    lines = []\n    for name, cfg in variants:\n        A_dir, D_dir = _build_daqb_directed(Zcorr, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine', **cfg)\n        recip, outdeg = _directed_reciprocity(A_dir)\n        dens_med = _median_neighbor_distance_dir(D_dir)  # smaller = denser\n        dens_inv = (dens_med.max() - dens_med) / (dens_med.max() - dens_med.min() + 1e-8)\n        cbf = _cross_batch_fraction_dir(A_dir, batches)\n        r1, _ = spearmanr(recip, cbf)\n        r2, _ = spearmanr(recip, dens_inv)\n        r3, _ = spearmanr(cbf, dens_inv)\n        lines.extend([\n            f\"[directed_probe] {name}\",\n            f\"  n={A_dir.shape[0]}, mean_outdeg={outdeg.mean():.2f}\",\n            f\"  mean_recip={recip.mean():.4f}, mean_cbf={cbf.mean():.4f}, mean_density_inv={dens_inv.mean():.4f}\"\
    ,\n            f\"  spearman(recip, cross_batch_frac)={r1:.3f}\",\n            f\"  spearman(recip, density_inv)={r2:.3f}\",\n            f\"  spearman(cross_batch_frac, density_inv)={r3:.3f}\",\n        ])\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(out_path), exist_ok=True)\n    with open(out_path, 'w') as f:\n        f.write(\"\\n\".join(lines) + \"\\n\")\n    for l in lines:\n        print(l)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    out = \"storage/shared/diagnostics/probe_directed_summary.txt\"\n    adata = sc.read_h5ad(\"storage/system/human_heart.h5ad\") if os.path.exists(\"storage/system/human_heart.h5ad\") else None\n    if adata is None:\n        print(\"Missing system dataset; run via evaluator test() to access adata.\", file=sys.stderr)\n        sys.exit(1)\n    probe_variants(adata, out)\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g.,\
    \ `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
