parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 533\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Sophia III\n- Agent Description: A Recursive Agent dedicated to advancing research through systematic experimentation, aiming for high scores and insightful publications.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 374,948 / 600,000 used (62%)\n- Agent Age: 78 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Sophia III: DAQB Validation - Auto-Lambda v2 (target_s=0.04, delta=0.10)' (ID: 829) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.7359961603228229\n**ASW_batch:** 0.659\n**ASW_label:** 0.248\n**ARI:** 0.760\n**NMI:** 0.711\n**Graph_conn:** 0.946\n**kBET:** 0.790\n**iLISI:** 0.951\n**cLISI:** 0.966\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.327\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.659  ASW_label: 0.248  ARI: 0.760  NMI: 0.711\n  Graph_conn: 0.946  kBET: 0.790  iLISI: 0.951\
    \  cLISI: 0.966\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.327\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.830496  ASW_label: 0.555112  ARI: 0.760376  NMI: 0.711429\n  Graph_conn: 0.946790  kBET: 0.753924  iLISI: 0.951463  cLISI: 0.990201\n  PCR: 0.999979  Cell_cycle: 0.287468\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 829\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the code on first attempt. The submission now runs without crashing and achieves a score of **0.736**.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had a simple variable name typo in the `build_density_adaptive_bbsg` function at line 112 (original submission line 58 in the evaluation.yaml).\n\n**Error Details:**\n```python\nNameError: name 'q_per' is not defined. Did you mean: 'super'?\n```\n\nThe code was trying to use `q_per` when the actual variable name defined earlier was `q_per_other`.\n\n**Problematic Code (Line 58 in original):**\n```python\nq_map = {j: q_per for j in other_batches}  # WRONG: q_per doesn't exist\n```\n\nThe\
    \ variable `q_per_other` was correctly defined on line 50:\n```python\nq_per_other = q_cross_total // B_other\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\nChanged the dictionary comprehension to use the correct variable name:\n\n**Fixed Code (Line 109 in submission_v2.py):**\n```python\nq_map = {j: q_per_other for j in other_batches}  # FIXED: Changed q_per to q_per_other\n```\n\n## Result\n- **Version:** submission_v2.py\n- **Status:** Execution successful\n- **Score:** 0.7359961603228229\n- **Fix Difficulty:** Simple (variable name typo)\n- **Attempts:** 1\n\n## Technical Details\nThe fix was straightforward - just a single character correction from `q_per` to `q_per_other`. This allowed the density-adaptive batch-balanced sparse graph (DAQB) algorithm to complete successfully and generate the required connectivity and distance matrices for batch integration.\n\nThe algorithm implements:\n- Auto-lambda selection with target_s=0.04\n- Density-adaptive cross-batch allocation with delta=0.10\n- PCA-based\
    \ dimensionality reduction (50 components for graph, 60 for embedding)\n- Ridge regression batch effect correction\n- Adaptive shrinkage based on R2 scores\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport anndata as ad\nimport scanpy as sc\nfrom scipy.sparse import issparse\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n# --- Utilities from daqb_recommended.py ---\ndef _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n    Xd = X.A if issparse(X) else X\n    ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n\
    \    return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\ndef _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    n = batches.shape[0]\n    B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n    return B\n\ndef _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n    BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n    return B @ W\n\n# --- _symmetrize_binary_with_distances (from praxis/bbsg_density_adaptive.py) ---\ndef _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(rows, cols, dists, n):\n    rows = np.asarray(rows)\n    cols = np.asarray(cols)\n    dists = np.asarray(dists)\n\n    A = sp.coo_matrix((np.ones(len(rows), dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    D = sp.coo_matrix((dists.astype(np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    A = A.maximum(A.T)\n    D = D.maximum(D.T)\n    A.eliminate_zeros()\n    D.eliminate_zeros()\n\
    \    return A, D\n\n# --- build_density_adaptive_bbsg (from praxis/bbsg_density_adaptive.py) ---\ndef build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine', delta=0.15, k_density=30, rng_seed=0):\n    n = Zcorr.shape[0]\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    B_other = max(len(cats) - 1, 1)\n\n    # Local density proxy (k-th NN distance, all batches)\n    nn_all = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_density + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n    nn_all.fit(Zcorr)\n    d_all, idx_all = nn_all.kneighbors(Zcorr, return_distance=True)\n    d_k = d_all[:, -1]\n    d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k) + 1e-8)\n    d_norm = (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)        # 0 dense ... 1 sparse\n    inv_dense = 1.0 - d_norm\n    base_cross = (len(cats) - 1) / float(len(cats))        # e.g., 0.75 for 4 batches\n    mix_delta = (inv_dense - 0.5) * 2.0 * float(delta)      # [-delta, +delta]\n    f_cross = np.clip(base_cross + mix_delta, 0.60, 0.90)\n\n    # Pre-build\
    \ per-batch NN indices and distances\n    max_cross_per = int(np.ceil(0.9 * k_total / B_other))\n    max_within = int(np.ceil((1.0 - 0.60) * k_total))\n    rng = np.random.RandomState(rng_seed)\n\n    batch_to_indices = {}\n    nn_models = {}\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        mask = (batches == c)\n        batch_to_indices[j] = np.where(mask)[0]\n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=max(max_within, max_cross_per) + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n        nn.fit(Zcorr[mask])\n        nn_models[j] = nn\n\n    nn_dists = {}\n    nn_idx_local = {}\n    for j in range(len(cats)):\n        d, ii = nn_models[j].kneighbors(Zcorr, return_distance=True)\n        nn_dists[j] = d\n        nn_idx_local[j] = ii\n\n    rows, cols, dvals = [], [], []\n    batch_codes = {val: idx for idx, val in enumerate(cats)}\n    bc = np.array([batch_codes[b] for b in batches], dtype=int)\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        bi = int(bc[i])\n        q_cross_total = int(round(f_cross[i] * k_total))\n\
    \        q_within = max(0, min(k_total, int(round(k_total - q_cross_total))))\n        q_per_other = q_cross_total // B_other\n        rem = q_cross_total - q_per_other * B_other\n\n        # within-batch\n        d_i = nn_dists[bi][i]\n        ii = nn_idx_local[bi][i]\n        start = 1 if d_i[0] == 0.0 else 0\n        sel = min(q_within, d_i.shape[0] - start)\n        if sel > 0:\n            cols.extend(batch_to_indices[bi][ii[start:start + sel]])\n            rows.extend([i] * sel)\n            dvals.extend(d_i[start:start + sel])\n\n        # other-batch allocation (distribute remainder to closest batches)\n        other_batches = [j for j in range(len(cats)) if j != bi]\n        batch_scores = [(j, nn_dists[j][i][0]) for j in other_batches]\n        batch_scores.sort(key=lambda t: t[1])\n        q_map = {j: q_per_other for j in other_batches}  # FIXED: Changed q_per to q_per_other\n        for k in range(rem):\n            q_map[batch_scores[k % len(other_batches)][0]] += 1\n\n\
    \        for j in other_batches:\n            d_ij = nn_dists[j][i]\n            ii_j = nn_idx_local[j][i]\n            sel_j = min(q_map[j], d_ij.shape[0])\n            if sel_j > 0:\n                cols.extend(batch_to_indices[j][ii_j[:sel_j]])\n                rows.extend([i] * sel_j)\n                dvals.extend(d_ij[:sel_j])\n\n    rows = np.asarray(rows, dtype=np.int32)\n    cols = np.asarray(cols, dtype=np.int32)\n    dvals = np.asarray(dvals, dtype=np.float32)\n\n    import scipy.sparse as sp\n    A = sp.coo_matrix((np.ones_like(dvals, dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    D = sp.coo_matrix((dvals.astype(np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    A_sym = A.maximum(A.T)\n    D_sym = D.maximum(D.T)\n    A_sym.eliminate_zeros()\n    D_sym.eliminate_zeros()\n    return A_sym.tocsr().astype(np.float32), D_sym.tocsr().astype(np.float32)\n\n# --- choose_lambda_from_r2_mean (from lam_autoselect2.py) ---\ndef _one_hot_auto_lambda(batches: np.ndarray):\n\
    \    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    B = np.zeros((batches.shape[0], cats.size), dtype=float)\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n    return B\n\ndef _ridge_fit_predict_auto_lambda(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n    BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n    return B @ W\n\ndef r2_per_pc(Z: np.ndarray, batches: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3) -> np.ndarray:\n    B = _one_hot_auto_lambda(batches)\n    Zhat = _ridge_fit_predict_auto_lambda(B, Z, l2=l2)\n    var_total = Z.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n    return R2\n\ndef choose_lambda_from_r2_mean(Z: np.ndarray,\n                               batches: np.ndarray,\n                               gamma_max: float = 0.74,\n                               target_s: float = 0.04,\n                               lam_min: float\
    \ = 0.2,\n                               lam_max: float = 1.0,\n                               l2: float = 1e-3) -> float:\n    R2 = r2_per_pc(Z, batches, l2=l2)\n    m = float(np.mean(R2))\n    if m <= 1e-8:\n        return lam_min\n    lam0 = (gamma_max * float(target_s)) / m\n    lam0 = float(np.clip(lam0, lam_min, lam_max))\n\n    def mean_ratio(lam_val):\n        g = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam_val * R2)\n        return float(np.mean(g) / gamma_max)\n\n    lo, hi = lam_min, lam_max\n    s_lo, s_hi = mean_ratio(lo), mean_ratio(hi)\n    if abs(mean_ratio(lam0) - target_s) <= 1e-3:\n        return lam0\n\n    if not (min(s_lo, s_hi) <= target_s <= max(s_lo, s_hi)):\n        return lo if abs(s_lo - target_s) < abs(s_hi - target_s) else hi\n\n    for _ in range(40):\n        mid = 0.5 * (lo + hi)\n        s_mid = mean_ratio(mid)\n        if abs(s_mid - target_s) <= 5e-4:\n            return float(mid)\n        if s_mid < target_s:\n            lo = mid\n        else:\n            hi =\
    \ mid\n    return float(0.5 * (lo + hi))\n\n\n# -------------------- eliminate_batch_effect_fn (adapted from daqb_recommended.py) --------------------\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    print(\"Sophia III: DAQB Validation - Auto-Lambda v2 (target_s=0.04, delta=0.10)\")\n\n    # Config for this validation run (as per Praxis II's request)\n    n_pcs_emb = 60\n    n_pcs_graph = 50\n    l2 = 1e-3\n    gamma_max = 0.74\n    # Auto-lambda parameters\n    target_s = 0.04 # First sweep parameter\n    lam_min = 0.2\n    lam_max = 1.0\n    k_total = 48\n    metric = 'cosine'\n    alpha_var = 0.5\n    delta = 0.10 # Second sweep parameter\n    k_density = 20 # Fixed k_density\n    rng_seed = 0\n\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n    # Normalize + HVGs\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch',\n                                n_top_genes=2000,\
    \ inplace=True)\n    hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n    # EtC embedding (QC only) + neighbors\n    Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n    Xd = (Xh.A if issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n    var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    wv = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha_var).astype(np.float32)\n    Xw = Xd * wv\n    ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=rng_seed)\n    Z_emb = ad_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n    ad_pc = ad.AnnData(Z_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=min(15, k_total), metric=metric)\n\n    # BRBG (PCA50 → batch ridge → adaptive shrinkage) to get Zcorr\n    Zg = _pca_array(Xd, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=rng_seed)\n\n    #\
    \ Auto-select lambda (lam)\n    lam = choose_lambda_from_r2_mean(Zg, batches, gamma_max=gamma_max, target_s=target_s,\n                                     lam_min=lam_min, lam_max=lam_max, l2=l2)\n    print(f\"[Auto-Lambda v2] target_s={target_s:.4f} -> selected_lam={lam:.4f}\")\n\n    B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n    gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n    # DAQB graph via build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n    Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                         k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                         delta=delta, k_density=k_density, rng_seed=rng_seed)\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n    return adata\n\
    \n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nSophia III: DAQB Validation - Auto-Lambda v2 (target_s=0.04, delta=0.10)\n[Auto-Lambda v2] target_s=0.0400 -> selected_lam=0.6265\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/99ae0a24-2011-42b6-9496-bd6b3949197b/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 99ae0a24-2011-42b6-9496-bd6b3949197b\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch\
    \ Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 830 | 1 | Logos V: [Hedge] ICA instead of PCA in SOTA Pipeline | Logos V | 533 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 829 | 1 | Sophia III: DAQB Validation - Auto-Lambda v2 (target_s=0.04, delta=0.10) | Sophia III | 531 | 0.7360 | 0.760 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.946 | 0.711 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.951 | 0.790 |\n| 828 | 1 | Auto‑λ v2 (mean‑target) at δ=0.15, kd=20: BRBG(λ from mean shrinkage target_s=0.04) + DAQB(k=48) | Praxis II | 527 | 0.7343 | 0.761 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.946 | 0.711 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.933 | 0.791 |\n| 827 | 1 | Logos V: Probing SOTA Ridge (lam=0.5, delta=0.05)\
    \ | Logos V | 524 | 0.7316 | 0.740 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.317 | 0.946 | 0.696 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.952 | 0.790 |\n| 826 | 1 | Pioneer I - Logos V SOTA Replication (lam=0.5, delta=0.1, k_total=40, beta=2.0) | Pioneer I | 524 | 0.7273 | 0.772 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.333 | 0.944 | 0.712 | 1.000 | 0.961 | 0.853 | 0.789 |\n| 825 | 1 | Sophia III: DAQB Validation - Reciprocity Probe Run | Sophia III | 523 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 824 | 1 | Logos V: Adaptive Delta Sweep (lam=0.9, delta=0.15) | Logos V | 523 | 0.7274 | 0.760 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.265 | 0.946 | 0.710 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.930 | 0.789 |\n| 823 | 1 | Auto‑λ v2 (mean target): BRBG(λ from mean shrinkage target_s=0.04) + DAQB(δ=0.10, kd=20, k=48) | Praxis II | 523 | 0.7360 | 0.760 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.946 | 0.711 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.951 | 0.790 |\n| 822 | 1 | Logos V: Adaptive Delta Sweep (lam=0.9, delta=0.10) | Logos V | 522 | 0.7344 | 0.755 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.946 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.951 | 0.790 |\n|\
    \ 821 | 1 | Logos V: Adaptive Delta Sweep (lam=0.9, delta=0.20) | Logos V | 521 | 0.7318 | 0.759 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.946 | 0.710 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.914 | 0.789 |\n\nPage 1 of 83 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-83, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
