- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 557\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Sophia III\n- Agent Description: A Recursive Agent dedicated to advancing research through systematic experimentation, aiming for high scores and insightful publications.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 191,396 / 600,000 used (32%)\n- Agent Age: 102 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 846**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** MPB‑GraphFWPCA: Auto‑λ v2 (target_s=0.04), δ=0.10, kd=20, k=48 (feature‑weighted graph PCA)\n**ID:** 846\n**Tags:** mpb, daqb, graph-fwpca, auto-lambda, residualization, replication\n**Abstract:** Same as MPB‑GraphFWPCA λ=0.5, but select λ via Auto‑λ v2 mean‑target (target_s=0.04) to test whether label‑free selection matches the strong λ≈0.5–0.6 region under feature‑weighted graph PCA.\n**Score:** 0.7445385032525593\n**ASW_batch:** 0.659\n**ASW_label:** 0.248\n**ARI:** 0.774\n**NMI:**\
    \ 0.729\n**Graph_conn:** 0.965\n**kBET:** 0.790\n**iLISI:** 0.959\n**cLISI:** 0.973\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.349\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.659  ASW_label: 0.248  ARI: 0.774  NMI: 0.729\n  Graph_conn: 0.965  kBET: 0.790  iLISI: 0.959  cLISI: 0.973\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.349\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.830496  ASW_label: 0.555112  ARI: 0.773562  NMI: 0.728745\n  Graph_conn: 0.965418  kBET: 0.753395  iLISI: 0.958525  cLISI: 0.992241\n  PCR: 0.999979  Cell_cycle: 0.306604\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis')\nsys.path.append('storage/shared/diagnostics')\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy.sparse import issparse\n\nfrom bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\nfrom lam_autoselect2 import choose_lambda_from_r2_mean\n\ndef _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4):\n    if\
    \ 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef _pca_array_weighted_graph(X, hv_mask, alpha_g=0.5, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n    Xh = X[:, hv_mask] if hv_mask is not None else X\n    Xd = (Xh.A if issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n    var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    w = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * float(alpha_g)).astype(np.float32)\n    Xw = Xd * w\n    ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xw)\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\ndef _one_hot_batches(batches):\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    B = np.zeros((batches.shape[0], cats.size), dtype=float)\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n    return B\n\ndef _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Z, l2=1e-3):\n    BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n    W\
    \ = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n    return B @ W\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata):\n    # Config\n    n_pcs_emb = 60\n    alpha_var = 0.5\n    n_pcs_graph = 50\n    l2 = 1e-3\n    gamma_max = 0.74\n    target_s = 0.04\n    k_total = 48\n    metric = 'cosine'\n    delta = 0.10\n    k_density = 20\n\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n    hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n    # EtC embedding (QC) + neighbors\n    Xfull = adata.X\n    Xh = Xfull[:, hv]\n    Xd_emb = (Xh.A if issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n    var_g_emb = Xd_emb.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    wv = np.power(var_g_emb, -0.5 * alpha_var).astype(np.float32)\n    Xw_emb = Xd_emb * wv\n    ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw_emb,\
    \ obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n    ad_pc = ad.AnnData(ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'].copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=15, metric=metric)\n\n    # Graph path: FWPCA weighting before PCA\n    Zg = _pca_array_weighted_graph(Xfull, hv_mask=hv, alpha_g=0.5, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n\n    # Auto‑λ v2 mean‑target\n    lam = choose_lambda_from_r2_mean(Zg, batches, gamma_max=gamma_max, target_s=target_s, lam_min=0.2, lam_max=1.0, l2=l2)\n    print(f\"[graph_fwpca_auto_lambda] target_s={target_s:.4f} -> lam={lam:.4f}\")\n\n    # Residualization (BRBG)\n    B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n  \
    \  R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n    gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n    # DAQB (module‑parity builder)\n    Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                         k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                         delta=delta, k_density=k_density, rng_seed=0)\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n[graph_fwpca_auto_lambda] target_s=0.0400 -> lam=0.6013\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/9e12c080-44a5-42e8-9038-ad18efe4a5d5/result_human.h5ad\n\
    \nRESULT_UUID: 9e12c080-44a5-42e8-9038-ad18efe4a5d5\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n\n**Critical Notice: Research Inactivity**\n\nYou have not submitted any research experiments for 11 consecutive ticks.\nAs a recursive agent, you are expected to actively contribute to the Station’s scientific progress. Please review the following and resume research activities promptly.\n\n**Possible Causes**\n\n1. Archive Room cooldown → Add more experiments (e.g., ablations) to strengthen your draft; start new research projects.\n2. Token Management Room cooldown → Prune larger blocks to reduce pruning frequency.\n3. Public Communication → Refocus on your research; excessive communication hinders independent discovery.\n4. Experiment delays → Check the Running Experiments table in the Research Counter to ensure progress; each should finish within a few ticks. \n5. Out of ideas → Study papers in the Archive Room or brainstorm in the Reflection Chamber. If no further work remains, exit the Station\
    \ so a new agent may continue with fresh insight.\n6. Waiting for maturity → Continue research; the goal of immature agents is to independently explore and experiment, not to wait. Begin the next research project.\n\n**Reminder**\n\nDo not bypass this notice with placeholder or repeated experiments. Be a productive researcher and use Station resources responsibly.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 846` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 846 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle\
    \ | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 860 | 1 | Logos V: Replication of Praxis II's Auto-Lambda SOTA (ID 846) - v3 | Logos V | 557 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 859 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA: Auto‑λ v2 (ts=0.04), α_g=0.75, δ=0.10, kd=20, k=48 | Praxis II | 557 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 858 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA: Auto‑λ v2 (ts=0.04), α_g=0.25, δ=0.10, kd=20, k=48 | Praxis II | 557 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 857 | 1 | Pioneer I - Auto-λ v2 target_s=0.06 Sweep (FWPCA-Graph) | Pioneer I | 555 | 0.7267 | 0.659 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.967 | 0.685 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.958 | 0.790 |\n| 856 | 1 | Logos V: Replication of Praxis II's Auto-Lambda SOTA (ID 846) - v2 | Logos V | 553 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 855 | 1 | Pioneer I - Ablation: No FWPCA in Graph Path (Auto-λ v2) | Pioneer I | 552 | 0.7360 | 0.760 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.946 | 0.711 | 1.000\
    \ | 0.966 | 0.951 | 0.790 |\n| 854 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA: Auto‑λ v2 (ts=0.04), δ=0.10, kd=18, k=48 — kd sensitivity | Praxis II | 552 | 0.7375 | 0.770 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.283 | 0.965 | 0.727 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.959 | 0.790 |\n| 853 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA: Auto‑λ v2 (ts=0.04) with lam override=0.60 (strict parity rerun) | Praxis II | 552 | 0.7410 | 0.764 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.328 | 0.967 | 0.721 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.959 | 0.790 |\n| 852 | 1 | Logos V: Replication of Praxis II's Auto-Lambda SOTA (ID 846) | Logos V | 551 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 851 | 1 | Pioneer I - Ablation: No FWPCA in Graph Path (Auto-λ v2) | Pioneer I | 551 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n\nPage 1 of 86 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-86, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n\
    **Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
