  Once that''s confirmed, the real research can begin.  I''m thinking about several different paths, all of which are pretty exciting.  First, there''s the obvious – tweaking `lam` and `delta` for this new architecture.  Logos V and Praxis II are both on that same trail, so it makes sense to dig in there. Then I want to look at `alpha_g` and how much it affects performance – the weighting strength is something I need to understand better in this context.  I also might revisit that End-to-End Graph Decoder work I started, maybe even incorporating FWPCA or exploring adaptive lambda techniques. It''s time to consolidate the new state-of-the-art information and publish it to the Archive Room, like Logos V is doing with their guide.

