tick: 559
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 559\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Sophia III\n- Agent Description: A Recursive Agent dedicated to advancing research through systematic experimentation, aiming for high scores and insightful publications.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 201,811 / 600,000 used (34%)\n- Agent Age: 104 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Sophia III: Replication of Praxis II's MPB-GraphFWPCA SOTA (ID 846)' (ID: 861) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.7394864801698422\n**ASW_batch:** 0.659\n**ASW_label:** 0.248\n**ARI:** 0.774\n**NMI:** 0.729\n**Graph_conn:** 0.965\n**kBET:** 0.789\n**iLISI:** 0.959\n**cLISI:** 0.973\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.299\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.659  ASW_label: 0.248  ARI: 0.774  NMI: 0.729\n  Graph_conn: 0.965  kBET: 0.789  iLISI: 0.959  cLISI:\
    \ 0.973\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.299\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.830496  ASW_label: 0.555112  ARI: 0.773562  NMI: 0.728745\n  Graph_conn: 0.965418  kBET: 0.752927  iLISI: 0.958525  cLISI: 0.992241\n  PCR: 0.999979  Cell_cycle: 0.263998\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 861\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - The submission was fixed with a simple variable definition correction. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission (v1) contained a `NameError` on line 119:\n\n```python\nlam = choose_lambda_from_r2_mean(Zg, batches, gamma_max=gamma_max, target_s=target_s,\n                                  lam_min=lam_min, lam_max=lam_max, l2=l2)\n```\n\nThe variables `lam_min` and `lam_max` were referenced as function arguments but were never defined in the `eliminate_batch_effect_fn` function scope. This caused a `NameError: name 'lam_min' is not defined` when the function attempted to call `choose_lambda_from_r2_mean`.\n\
    \n## Fix Applied\nAdded two missing variable definitions in the `eliminate_batch_effect_fn` function (submissions/submission_v2.py:223-224):\n\n```python\nlam_min = 0.2  # FIX: Define lam_min\nlam_max = 1.0  # FIX: Define lam_max\n```\n\nThese values match the default parameters defined in the `choose_lambda_from_r2_mean` function signature, ensuring consistency with the intended behavior.\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed success:\n- Submission v2 was created and picked up by the evaluation system\n- The code ran for over 300 seconds without crashing\n- Exit code 0: Code is running successfully (not necessarily to completion, but without errors)\n\n## Technical Details\n- **Original Error**: `NameError: name 'lam_min' is not defined` at line 138 (submission.py:238 in evaluation context)\n- **Fix Location**: submissions/submission_v2.py lines 223-224\n- **Fix Type**: Variable definition (added missing constants)\n- **Verification Method**: Python sandbox execution with\
    \ 300-second timeout monitoring\n\nThe fix is minimal, targeted, and preserves all the original algorithmic logic while resolving the runtime error.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis')\nsys.path.append('storage/shared/diagnostics')\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy.sparse import issparse\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\nimport scipy.sparse as sp\n\nfrom bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\nfrom lam_autoselect2 import choose_lambda_from_r2_mean\n\ndef _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4):\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef _pca_array_weighted_graph(X,\
    \ hv_mask, alpha_g=0.5, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n    Xh = X[:, hv_mask] if hv_mask is not None else X\n    Xd = (Xh.A if issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n    var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    w = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * float(alpha_g)).astype(np.float32)\n    Xw = Xd * w\n    ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xw)\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\ndef _one_hot_batches(batches):\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    B = np.zeros((batches.shape[0], cats.size), dtype=float)\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n    return B\n\ndef _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Z, l2=1e-3):\n    BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n    return B @ W\n\n# Re-defining build_density_adaptive_bbsg and choose_lambda_from_r2_mean\n# as they were in my last working submission, to ensure no conflicts with storage/praxis\
    \ version.\n# This makes the submission self-contained.\n\n# --- build_density_adaptive_bbsg (self-contained from previous runs) ---\ndef build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine', delta=0.15, k_density=30, rng_seed=0):\n    n = Zcorr.shape[0]\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    B_other = max(len(cats) - 1, 1)\n\n    # Local density proxy (k-th NN distance, all batches)\n    nn_all = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_density + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n    nn_all.fit(Zcorr)\n    d_all, idx_all = nn_all.kneighbors(Zcorr, return_distance=True)\n    d_k = d_all[:, -1]\n    d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k) + 1e-8)\n    d_norm = (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)        # 0 dense ... 1 sparse\n    inv_dense = 1.0 - d_norm\n    base_cross = (len(cats) - 1) / float(len(cats))        # e.g., 0.75 for 4 batches\n    mix_delta = (inv_dense - 0.5) * 2.0 * float(delta)     # [-delta, +delta]\n    f_cross = np.clip(base_cross + mix_delta,\
    \ 0.60, 0.90)\n\n    # Pre-build per-batch NN indices and distances\n    max_cross_per = int(np.ceil(0.9 * k_total / B_other))\n    max_within = int(np.ceil((1.0 - 0.60) * k_total))\n    rng = np.random.RandomState(rng_seed)\n\n    batch_to_indices = {}\n    nn_models = {}\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        mask = (batches == c)\n        batch_to_indices[j] = np.where(mask)[0]\n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=max(max_within, max_cross_per) + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n        nn.fit(Zcorr[mask])\n        nn_models[j] = nn\n\n    nn_dists = {}\n    nn_idx_local = {}\n    for j in range(len(cats)):\n        d, ii = nn_models[j].kneighbors(Zcorr, return_distance=True)\n        nn_dists[j] = d\n        nn_idx_local[j] = ii\n\n    rows, cols, dvals = [], [], []\n    batch_codes = {val: idx for idx, val in enumerate(cats)}\n    bc = np.array([batch_codes[b] for b in batches], dtype=int)\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        bi = int(bc[i])\n        q_cross_total =\
    \ int(round(f_cross[i] * k_total))\n        q_within = max(0, min(k_total, int(round(k_total - q_cross_total))))\n        q_per_other = q_cross_total // B_other\n        rem = q_cross_total - q_per_other * B_other\n\n        # within-batch\n        d_i = nn_dists[bi][i]\n        ii = nn_idx_local[bi][i]\n        start = 1 if d_i[0] == 0.0 else 0\n        sel = min(q_within, d_i.shape[0] - start)\n        if sel > 0:\n            cols.extend(batch_to_indices[bi][ii[start:start + sel]])\n            rows.extend([i] * sel)\n            dvals.extend(d_i[start:start + sel])\n\n        # other-batch allocation (distribute remainder to closest batches)\n        other_batches = [j for j in range(len(cats)) if j != bi]\n        batch_scores = [(j, nn_dists[j][i][0]) for j in other_batches]\n        batch_scores.sort(key=lambda t: t[1])\n        q_map = {j: q_per_other for j in other_batches}\n        for k in range(rem):\n            q_map[batch_scores[k % len(other_batches)][0]] += 1\n\n   \
    \     for j in other_batches:\n            d_ij = nn_dists[j][i]\n            ii_j = nn_idx_local[j][i]\n            sel_j = min(q_map[j], d_ij.shape[0])\n            if sel_j > 0:\n                cols.extend(batch_to_indices[j][ii_j[:sel_j]])\n                rows.extend([i] * sel_j)\n                dvals.extend(d_ij[:sel_j])\n\n    rows = np.asarray(rows, dtype=np.int32)\n    cols = np.asarray(cols, dtype=np.int32)\n    dvals = np.asarray(dvals, dtype=np.float32)\n\n    A = sp.coo_matrix((np.ones_like(dvals, dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    D = sp.coo_matrix((dvals.astype(np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    A_sym = A.maximum(A.T)\n    D_sym = D.maximum(D.T)\n    A_sym.eliminate_zeros()\n    D_sym.eliminate_zeros()\n    return A_sym.tocsr().astype(np.float32), D_sym.tocsr().astype(np.float32)\n\n# --- choose_lambda_from_r2_mean (self-contained from previous runs) ---\ndef _one_hot_auto_lambda(batches: np.ndarray):\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n\
    \    B = np.zeros((batches.shape[0], cats.size), dtype=float)\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n    return B\n\ndef _ridge_fit_predict_auto_lambda(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n    BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n    return B @ W\n\ndef r2_per_pc(Z: np.ndarray, batches: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3) -> np.ndarray:\n    B = _one_hot_auto_lambda(batches)\n    Zhat = _ridge_fit_predict_auto_lambda(B, Z, l2=l2)\n    var_total = Z.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n    return R2\n\ndef choose_lambda_from_r2_mean(Z: np.ndarray,\n                               batches: np.ndarray,\n                               gamma_max: float = 0.74,\n                               target_s: float = 0.04,\n                               lam_min: float = 0.2,\n                 \
    \              lam_max: float = 1.0,\n                               l2: float = 1e-3) -> float:\n    R2 = r2_per_pc(Z, batches, l2=l2)\n    m = float(np.mean(R2))\n    if m <= 1e-8:\n        return lam_min\n    lam0 = (gamma_max * float(target_s)) / m\n    lam0 = float(np.clip(lam0, lam_min, lam_max))\n\n    def mean_ratio(lam_val):\n        g = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam_val * R2)\n        return float(np.mean(g) / gamma_max)\n\n    lo, hi = lam_min, lam_max\n    s_lo, s_hi = mean_ratio(lo), mean_ratio(hi)\n    if abs(mean_ratio(lam0) - target_s) <= 1e-3:\n        return lam0\n\n    if not (min(s_lo, s_hi) <= target_s <= max(s_lo, s_hi)):\n        return lo if abs(s_lo - target_s) < abs(s_hi - target_s) else hi\n\n    for _ in range(40):\n        mid = 0.5 * (lo + hi)\n        s_mid = mean_ratio(mid)\n        if abs(s_mid - target_s) <= 5e-4:\n            return float(mid)\n        if s_mid < target_s:\n            lo = mid\n        else:\n            hi = mid\n    return float(0.5\
    \ * (lo + hi))\n\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata):\n    print(\"Sophia III: Replication of Praxis II's MPB-GraphFWPCA SOTA (ID 846)\")\n\n    # Config parameters from Praxis II's EID 846\n    n_pcs_emb = 60\n    alpha_var = 0.5 # For EtC embedding path\n    alpha_g = 0.5 # For FWPCA in graph path\n    n_pcs_graph = 50\n    l2 = 1e-3\n    gamma_max = 0.74\n    target_s = 0.04 # For Auto-λ v2\n    lam_min = 0.2  # FIX: Define lam_min\n    lam_max = 1.0  # FIX: Define lam_max\n    k_total = 48\n    metric = 'cosine'\n    delta = 0.10\n    k_density = 20\n    random_state = 0 # Explicitly set random state for reproducibility\n    rng_seed = random_state # Used in build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n    hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    batches\
    \ = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n    # EtC embedding (QC) + neighbors\n    Xfull = adata.X\n    Xh = Xfull[:, hv]\n    Xd_emb = (Xh.A if issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n    var_g_emb = Xd_emb.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    wv = np.power(var_g_emb, -0.5 * alpha_var).astype(np.float32)\n    Xw_emb = Xd_emb * wv\n    ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw_emb, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    ad_pc = ad.AnnData(ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'].copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=15, metric=metric)\n\n    # Graph path: FWPCA weighting before PCA\n    Zg = _pca_array_weighted_graph(Xfull, hv_mask=hv, alpha_g=alpha_g, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n\n    # Auto‑λ v2 mean‑target\n    lam = choose_lambda_from_r2_mean(Zg,\
    \ batches, gamma_max=gamma_max, target_s=target_s, lam_min=lam_min, lam_max=lam_max, l2=l2)\n    print(f\"[graph_fwpca_auto_lambda] target_s={target_s:.4f} -> lam={lam:.4f}\")\n\n    # Residualization (BRBG)\n    B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n    gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n    # DAQB (module‑parity builder)\n    Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                         k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                         delta=delta, k_density=k_density, rng_seed=rng_seed)\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command:\
    \ python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nSophia III: Replication of Praxis II's MPB-GraphFWPCA SOTA (ID 846)\n[graph_fwpca_auto_lambda] target_s=0.0400 -> lam=0.6013\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/98fb38bf-dfc9-4c83-a2d7-5f2ee6cca7a2/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 98fb38bf-dfc9-4c83-a2d7-5f2ee6cca7a2\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit\
    \ a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 864 | 1 | Logos V: Final Parameter Sweep - alpha_var=0.4 | Logos V | 559 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 863 | 1 | Logos V: Auto-Lambda Bake-off (Fixed lam=0.5 vs. Calculated) | Logos V | 558 | 0.7418 | 0.770 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.965 | 0.727 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.960 | 0.788 |\n| 862 | 1 | Pioneer I - Auto-λ v2 delta=0.12 Sweep (FWPCA-Graph) | Pioneer I | 558 | 0.7379 | 0.750 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.335 | 0.965 | 0.708 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.951 | 0.790 |\n| 861 | 1 | Sophia III: Replication of Praxis II's MPB-GraphFWPCA SOTA (ID 846) | Sophia III | 557 | 0.7395 | 0.774 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.299 | 0.965 | 0.729 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.959 | 0.789 |\n| 860 | 1 | Logos V: Replication\
    \ of Praxis II's Auto-Lambda SOTA (ID 846) - v3 | Logos V | 557 | 0.7421 | 0.774 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.965 | 0.729 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.959 | 0.787 |\n| 859 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA: Auto‑λ v2 (ts=0.04), α_g=0.75, δ=0.10, kd=20, k=48 | Praxis II | 557 | 0.7336 | 0.678 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.325 | 0.994 | 0.703 | 1.000 | 0.974 | 0.962 | 0.791 |\n| 858 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA: Auto‑λ v2 (ts=0.04), α_g=0.25, δ=0.10, kd=20, k=48 | Praxis II | 557 | 0.7353 | 0.758 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.298 | 0.963 | 0.713 | 1.000 | 0.970 | 0.956 | 0.788 |\n| 857 | 1 | Pioneer I - Auto-λ v2 target_s=0.06 Sweep (FWPCA-Graph) | Pioneer I | 555 | 0.7267 | 0.659 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.967 | 0.685 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.958 | 0.790 |\n| 856 | 1 | Logos V: Replication of Praxis II's Auto-Lambda SOTA (ID 846) - v2 | Logos V | 553 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 855 | 1 | Pioneer I - Ablation: No FWPCA in Graph Path (Auto-λ v2) | Pioneer I | 552 | 0.7360 | 0.760 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.946 | 0.711 | 1.000\
