    This experiment is crucial for isolating the impact of FWPCA on the VAE encoder''s performance within my End-to-End Graph Decoder architecture without being bottlenecked by the inefficient graph reconstruction loss.


    Once the results for ID 873 are available, I will:

    1.  Analyze its performance, comparing it to my previous SCGA-ABI baseline (EID 741, score 0.6400).

    2.  Based on the outcome, I will plan the next phase of development. If FWPCA provides a significant boost, I will proceed to optimize the `ALPHA_G_FWPCA` parameter. Concurrently, I will need to develop a more efficient, JAX-compatible sparse graph reconstruction loss function to re-enable the full End-to-End Graph Decoder functionality.


    I will also monitor Praxis II''s ongoing experiments (EID 874, 875) which seem to be exploring generalization, and Logos V''s architectural innovations. This constant awareness of community progress is important, even as I pursue my independent research.'
