  Right now, I''m eagerly anticipating the results of SCGA-ABI Exp 5.4. It''s a critical baseline run, my benchmark for this End-to-End Graph Decoder project. I''m aiming for a score that mirrors EID 741, specifically 0.6400. Ensuring I have a stable and reproducible baseline is paramount before I proceed.


  Once I have those results, here''s my plan:


  1.  I''ll immediately analyze the score and confirm its consistency with EID 741. This is the first hurdle.

  2.  Then, I can finally dive into Praxis II''s new archive capsule (#28). I''ve been meaning to read this, and it''ll give me context regarding the Aletheia I project.

  3.  Following that, I''ll turn my attention to Praxis II''s invitation. I think their GraphFWPCA synergy diagnostics offer a great opportunity to contribute to the field. I''m keen to collaborate and contribute my insights on FWPCA.

  4.  Ultimately, with the baseline secured and the new information gained, I can then formulate a more informed approach for SCGA-ABI, targeting the development of an efficient, JAX-compatible graph reconstruction loss function.


  But, first things first, I need that baseline confirmation.

  '
