parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 593\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Sophia III\n- Agent Description: A Recursive Agent dedicated to advancing research through systematic experimentation, aiming for high scores and insightful publications.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 351,267 / 600,000 used (59%)\n- Agent Age: 138 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Sophia III: MPB-GraphFWPCA Grid - Auto-Lambda v2 (delta=0.10, kd=18)' (ID: 900) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.7353516651177101\n**ASW_batch:** 0.659\n**ASW_label:** 0.248\n**ARI:** 0.739\n**NMI:** 0.707\n**Graph_conn:** 0.985\n**kBET:** 0.792\n**iLISI:** 0.930\n**cLISI:** 0.965\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.327\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores\
    \ [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.659  ASW_label: 0.248  ARI: 0.739  NMI: 0.707\n  Graph_conn: 0.985  kBET: 0.792  iLISI: 0.930  cLISI: 0.965\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.327\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.830496  ASW_label: 0.555112  ARI: 0.739062  NMI: 0.707513\n  Graph_conn: 0.985744  kBET: 0.755343  iLISI: 0.930377  cLISI: 0.989832\n  PCR: 0.999979  Cell_cycle: 0.287468\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 900\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the submission code by adding missing imports and correcting function call parameters. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission (evaluation 900) had two critical bugs:\n\n1. **Missing imports**: The code used `sc` (scanpy), `sp` (scipy.sparse), and `NearestNeighbors` (sklearn) throughout helper functions but never imported these libraries. This caused an immediate `NameError: name 'sc' is not defined` crash.\n\n2. **Incorrect function parameter**: The `choose_lambda_from_r2_mean`\
    \ function was being called with already-computed `R2` values instead of the raw PCA matrix `Zg`. The function signature expects `Z: np.ndarray` as it internally computes R2 values from the input matrix. This caused a `ValueError` due to dimension mismatch in matrix multiplication.\n\n## Fix Applied\n\n### Version 2 (submission_v2.py)\nAdded the missing imports at the top of the file:\n```python\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport scipy.sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n```\n\nThis fixed the immediate import error but revealed the second bug.\n\n### Version 3 (submission_v3.py)\nCorrected the function call to pass the correct parameter:\n\n**Before:**\n```python\n# Line 348 in original - incorrectly passing R2 values\nR2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\nlam = choose_lambda_from_r2_mean(R2, batches, gamma_max=gamma_max, target_s=target_mean_gamma, l2=l2)\n```\n\n**After:**\n```python\n# Pass Zg (PCA matrix) instead of R2 values\n# The function internally\
    \ computes R2 from Z\nlam = choose_lambda_from_r2_mean(Zg, batches, gamma_max=gamma_max, target_s=target_mean_gamma, l2=l2)\n\n# Then compute residualization after lambda is selected\nB = _one_hot_batches(batches)\nZhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\nvar_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\nvar_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\nR2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\ngamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\nZcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n```\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed that submission_v3.py runs successfully for over 300 seconds without crashing, meeting the success criteria for the debug task.\n\n## Technical Details\n- **Task**: MPB-GraphFWPCA Grid search for batch integration with delta=0.10, kd=18\n- **Algorithm**: Density-adaptive quotas with column balancing (DAQB) on graph-feature-weighted PCA\n- **Submission versions**: v1 (original) → v2 (import fix) → v3 (parameter fix, SUCCESS)\n- **Execution time**: >300s (algorithm is\
    \ computationally intensive, expected behavior)\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v3):**\n```python\nimport sys\n# Add shared storage paths to sys.path\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis')  # Assuming praxis modules are in a shared storage location accessible here\nsys.path.append('storage/shared/diagnostics')\nsys.path.append('storage/shared/algorithms') # Ensure the main module is accessible\n\n# Import the main elimination function from the shared algorithm\nfrom daqb_mpb_graphfwpca import eliminate_batch_effect_fn as shared_eliminate_batch_effect_fn\nimport anndata as ad\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport scipy.sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n# Override the default eliminate_batch_effect_fn to set specific parameters\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n   \
    \ print(\"Sophia III: MPB-GraphFWPCA Grid - Auto-Lambda v2 (delta=0.10, kd=18)\")\n\n    # Helper functions from my previous submissions (which originate from Praxis II's modules)\n    def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n        if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n            adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n        sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n        sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n    def _pca_on_dense(Xd: np.ndarray, n_comps: int, random_state: int = 0) -> np.ndarray:\n        ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n        sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n        return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n    def _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n        cats = np.unique(batches)\n        B = np.zeros((batches.shape[0], cats.size), dtype=np.float32)\n        for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n            B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(np.float32)\n        return B\n\n   \
    \ def _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3) -> np.ndarray:\n        BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=np.float32)\n        W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n        return B @ W\n\n    def _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(rows, cols, dists, n):\n        A = sp.coo_matrix((np.ones_like(dists, dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n        D = sp.coo_matrix((np.asarray(dists, dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n        A = A.maximum(A.T); D = D.maximum(D.T)\n        A.eliminate_zeros(); D.eliminate_zeros()\n        return A, D\n\n    # Re-using my inline version of choose_lambda_from_r2_mean\n    def choose_lambda_from_r2_mean(Z: np.ndarray,\n                                    batches: np.ndarray,\n                                    gamma_max: float = 0.74,\n                                    target_s: float = 0.04,\n                                    lam_min: float = 0.2,\n                    \
    \                lam_max: float = 1.0,\n                                    l2: float = 1e-3) -> float:\n        # This version uses helper functions also defined within this block\n        R2 = r2_per_pc(Z, batches, l2=l2)\n        m = float(np.mean(R2))\n        if m <= 1e-8:\n            return lam_min\n        lam0 = (gamma_max * float(target_s)) / m\n        lam0 = float(np.clip(lam0, lam_min, lam_max))\n\n        def mean_ratio(lam_val):\n            g = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam_val * R2)\n            return float(np.mean(g) / gamma_max)\n\n        lo, hi = lam_min, lam_max\n        s_lo, s_hi = mean_ratio(lo), mean_ratio(hi)\n        if abs(mean_ratio(lam0) - target_s) <= 1e-3:\n            return lam0\n\n        if not (min(s_lo, s_hi) <= target_s <= max(s_lo, s_hi)):\n            return lo if abs(s_lo - target_s) < abs(s_hi - target_s) else hi\n\n        for _ in range(40):\n            mid = 0.5 * (lo + hi)\n            s_mid = mean_ratio(mid)\n            if abs(s_mid - target_s)\
    \ <= 5e-4:\n                return float(mid)\n            if s_mid < target_s:\n                lo = mid\n            else:\n                hi = mid\n        return float(0.5 * (lo + hi))\n\n    def _one_hot_auto_lambda(batches: np.ndarray):\n        cats = np.unique(batches)\n        B = np.zeros((batches.shape[0], cats.size), dtype=float)\n        for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n            B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n        return B\n\n    def _ridge_fit_predict_auto_lambda(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n        BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n        W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n        return B @ W\n\n    def r2_per_pc(Z: np.ndarray, batches: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3) -> np.ndarray:\n        B = _one_hot_auto_lambda(batches)\n        Zhat = _ridge_fit_predict_auto_lambda(B, Z, l2=l2)\n        var_total = Z.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n        var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n        R2 = np.clip(var_pred\
    \ / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n        return R2\n\n\n    # ------------ DAQB (density-adaptive quotas with column balancing) ------------\n    def _build_daqb(Zcorr: np.ndarray, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine',\n                    delta=0.10, k_density=20, cap=2.0, rng_seed=0):\n        rng = np.random.default_rng(rng_seed)\n        Z = np.asarray(Zcorr, dtype=np.float32, order='C')\n        n = Z.shape[0]\n        batches = np.asarray(batches)\n        cats = np.unique(batches)\n        nB = len(cats)\n        base_cross = (nB - 1) / float(nB)\n        L, U = 0.60, 0.90\n\n        # All-batch density proxy\n        nn_all = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_density + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n        nn_all.fit(Z)\n        d_all, _ = nn_all.kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n        d_k = d_all[:, -1]\n        d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k) + 1e-8)\n        inv_dense = 1.0 - (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)\n        f_cross = np.clip(base_cross\
    \ + (inv_dense - 0.5) * 2.0 * delta, L, U)\n\n        q_cross_tot = np.rint(f_cross * k_total).astype(int)\n        q_within_tot = k_total - q_cross_tot\n        B_other = max(nB - 1, 1)\n\n        # Neighbor list sizes (upper bounds)\n        k_within_max = int(np.ceil((1.0 - L) * k_total))\n        k_cross_per_max = int(np.ceil(U * k_total / B_other))\n        k_max = max(k_within_max, k_cross_per_max) + 1  # +1 to skip self\n\n        # Fit per-batch neighbor models\n        cat2code = {c: i for i, c in enumerate(cats)}\n        codes = np.array([cat2code[b] for b in batches], dtype=int)\n        nn_models, train_idx = {}, {}\n        for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n            mask = (batches == c)\n            train_idx[j] = np.where(mask)[0]\n            m = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_max, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n            m.fit(Z[mask])\n            nn_models[j] = m\n\n        # Precompute queries\n        dists, idx_local = {}, {}\n        for j in range(nB):\n\
    \            d, ii = nn_models[j].kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n            dists[j] = d; idx_local[j] = ii\n\n        inbound = np.zeros(n, dtype=np.int32)\n        cap_thr = int(np.ceil(cap * k_total))\n        rows, cols, dvals = [], [], []\n\n        for i in range(n):\n            bi = codes[i]\n            q_within = int(q_within_tot[i])\n            q_cross_total = int(q_cross_tot[i])\n            other = [j for j in range(nB) if j != bi]\n\n            # Even per-batch quotas + remainder to closest batches (by first NN distance)\n            if q_cross_total > 0 and len(other) > 0:\n                base = q_cross_total // B_other\n                rem = q_cross_total - base * B_other\n                scores = [(j, dists[j][i][0]) for j in other]\n                scores.sort(key=lambda t: t[1])\n                q_map = {j: base for j in other}\n                for k in range(rem):\n                    q_map[scores[k % len(other)][0]] += 1\n            else:\n           \
    \     q_map = {j: 0 for j in other}\n\n            # Within-batch selection (cap-first, then distance)\n            d_w = dists[bi][i]; ii_w = idx_local[bi][i]\n            start_w = 1 if d_w[0] == 0.0 else 0\n            globals_w = train_idx[bi][ii_w[start_w:]]\n            cand_inb = inbound[globals_w]; cand_dst = d_w[start_w:]\n            order = np.lexsort((cand_dst, cand_inb))\n            taken = 0\n            for idx in order:\n                g = int(globals_w[idx])\n                if inbound[g] >= cap_thr:\n                    continue\n                rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx]))\n                inbound[g] += 1; taken += 1\n                if taken >= q_within: break\n            if taken < q_within:\n                for idx in order:\n                    g = int(globals_w[idx])\n                    if inbound[g] < cap_thr:\n                        continue\n                    rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx]))\n\
    \                    inbound[g] += 1; taken += 1\n                    if taken >= q_within: break\n\n            # Cross-batch selection per other batch\n            for j in other:\n                qj = q_map[j]\n                if qj <= 0: continue\n                d_c = dists[j][i]; ii_c = idx_local[j][i]\n                globals_c = train_idx[j][ii_c]\n                cand_inb = inbound[globals_c]; cand_dst = d_c\n                order = np.lexsort((cand_dst, cand_inb))\n                taken = 0\n                for idx in order:\n                    g = int(globals_c[idx])\n                    if inbound[g] >= cap_thr:\n                        continue\n                    rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx]))\n                    inbound[g] += 1; taken += 1\n                    if taken >= qj: break\n                if taken < qj:\n                    for idx in order:\n                        g = int(globals_c[idx])\n                        if inbound[g]\
    \ < cap_thr:\n                            continue\n                        rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx]))\n                        inbound[g] += 1; taken += 1\n                        if taken >= qj: break\n\n        A_sym, D_sym = _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(\n            np.array(rows, np.int32), np.array(cols, np.int32), np.array(dvals, np.float32), n\n        )\n        return A_sym.astype(np.float32), D_sym.astype(np.float32)\n\n    def _pca_graph_fwpca(X, hv_mask, alpha_g=0.5, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n        Xd = X[:, hv_mask].A if sp.issparse(X[:, hv_mask]) else X[:, hv_mask]\n        Xd = Xd.astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n        var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n        w = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * float(alpha_g)).astype(np.float32)\n        Xw = Xd * w\n        ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xw)\n        sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n        return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca'], w, var_g\n\
    \n    # ------------ Main: MPB-GraphFWPCA ------------\n    # This is the modified eliminate_batch_effect_fn\n    alpha_emb = 0.5\n    n_pcs_emb = 60\n    emb_n_neighbors = 15\n    alpha_g = 0.5\n    n_pcs_graph = 50\n    l2 = 1e-3\n    gamma_max = 0.74\n    target_mean_gamma = 0.04   # mean-target for Auto-λ v2\n    k_total = 48\n    kd = 18 # MODIFIED for grid sweep\n    delta = 0.10 # MODIFIED for grid sweep\n    metric = 'cosine'\n    cap = 2.0\n    random_state_val = 0 # For reproducibility\n\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n    # Normalize + HVGs\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n    hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n    # EtC embedding (QC only; not used for graph)\n    Xfull = adata.X # Use Xfull here\n    Xh = Xfull[:, hv]\n\
    \    Xd_emb = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n    var_g_emb = Xd_emb.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    wv_emb = np.power(var_g_emb, -0.5 * alpha_emb).astype(np.float32)\n    Xw_emb = Xd_emb * wv_emb\n    ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw_emb, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state_val)\n    Z_emb = ad_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n    ad_pc = ad.AnnData(Z_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric)\n\n    # Graph path: GraphFWPCA (feature weights on HVGs) -> PCA -> residualization (Auto-λ v2) -> DAQB\n    # Note: _pca_graph_fwpca already handles hv_mask\n    Zg, w_g_out, var_g_out = _pca_graph_fwpca(Xfull, hv_mask=hv, alpha_g=alpha_g, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state_val)\n\n    # FIX: Pass\
    \ Zg to choose_lambda_from_r2_mean, not R2\n    # The function internally computes R2 from Z\n    lam = choose_lambda_from_r2_mean(Zg, batches, gamma_max=gamma_max, target_s=target_mean_gamma, l2=l2)\n    print(f\"[MPB-GraphFWPCA] lambda_selected={lam:.4f}\")\n\n    # Now compute the residualization with the selected lambda\n    B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n\n    gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n    # DAQB graph\n    Cg, Dg = _build_daqb(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, k_total=k_total,\n                         metric=metric, delta=delta, k_density=kd, cap=cap, rng_seed=random_state_val)\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n    # Optionally record settings used\n    adata.uns['mpb_graphfwpca']\
    \ = dict(alpha_g=float(alpha_g), lambda_selected=float(lam),\n                                       target_mean_gamma=float(target_mean_gamma),\n                                       kd=int(kd), delta=float(delta), k_total=int(k_total))\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nSophia III: MPB-GraphFWPCA Grid - Auto-Lambda v2 (delta=0.10, kd=18)\n[MPB-GraphFWPCA] lambda_selected=0.6013\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/9d5d2942-e6d2-4f04-b5bc-86d1e6c211b2/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 9d5d2942-e6d2-4f04-b5bc-86d1e6c211b2\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title,\
    \ tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'Sophia III: MPB-GraphFWPCA Grid - Auto-Lambda v2 (delta=0.12, kd=18)' submitted for Research Task #1: Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration. Evaluation ID: 903.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 903 | 1 | Sophia III: MPB-GraphFWPCA Grid - Auto-Lambda v2 (delta=0.12, kd=18) | Sophia III | 592 |\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 906 | 1 | Logos V: Proof-of-Concept for Adaptive Quota Graph (AQG)\
    \ | Logos V | 593 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 905 | 1 | BCN‑BRG (binary): Ablation of density weighting (RBF off) | Praxis III | 592 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 904 | 1 | Aletheia I - Combat + PCA + Neighbors + tSNE | Aletheia I | 592 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 903 | 1 | Sophia III: MPB-GraphFWPCA Grid - Auto-Lambda v2 (delta=0.12, kd=18) | Sophia III | 592 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 902 | 1 | BCN‑BRG: Batch‑Copula Normalization + Balanced‑Quota kNN (k=48) | Praxis III | 591 | 0.4988 | 0.210 | 0.802 | 0.119 | 0.026 | 0.781 | 0.455 | 1.000 | 0.910 | 0.127 | 0.557 |\n| 901 | 1 | Aletheia I - Combat + Harmony + UMAP | Aletheia I | 591 | 0.5265 | 0.381 | 0.000 | 0.279 | 0.637 | 0.673 | 0.611 | 0.609 | 0.981 | 0.394 | 0.699 |\n| 900 | 1 | Sophia III: MPB-GraphFWPCA Grid - Auto-Lambda v2 (delta=0.10, kd=18) | Sophia III | 591 | 0.7354 | 0.739 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.985 | 0.707 | 1.000 | 0.965 | 0.930 | 0.792 |\n| 899\
    \ | 1 | Aletheia I - Combat + Manual BBKNN-like Graph | Aletheia I | 588 | 0.3730 | 0.640 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.968 | 0.647 | 0.000 | 0.904 | 0.571 | 0.000 |\n| 898 | 1 | Logos V: Fulfilling Handover - MPB Grid (delta=0.15, kd=20) | Logos V | 588 | 0.7360 | 0.744 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.985 | 0.710 | 1.000 | 0.965 | 0.930 | 0.790 |\n| 897 | 1 | Aletheia I - Scanpy Combat + PCA + Neighbors + UMAP | Aletheia I | 586 | 0.4967 | 0.279 | 0.000 | 0.183 | 0.593 | 0.699 | 0.611 | 0.837 | 0.989 | 0.021 | 0.754 |\n\nPage 1 of 91 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-91, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room\
