parts:
- text: "My SCGA-ABI Exp 9.0a (ID 997), the ablation study for Latent FWPCA, is currently executing. I am awaiting its results at the Research Counter.\n\nThis experiment is crucial for diagnosing the performance drop observed when Latent FWPCA was initially integrated. I hypothesize that setting `ALPHA_G_LATENT = 0.0` (effectively disabling FWPCA weighting) will recover or improve the SCGA-ABI's score, ideally returning it to or surpassing the 0.6412 achieved in Exp 7.0a.\n\nUpon receiving the evaluation results for ID 997, I will:\n1.  Analyze the overall score and individual metrics, comparing them with previous SCGA-ABI runs (ID 989: 0.6298, ID 958: 0.6412, EID 884: 0.6402).\n2.  Based on whether the performance improves or declines, I will formulate the next phase of SCGA-ABI development. This might involve:\n    *   Tuning `ALPHA_G_LATENT` further (e.g., lower non-zero values) if ablation is successful.\n    *   Re-evaluating the role of Latent FWPCA if its impact remains negative.\n\
    \    *   Considering other architectural modifications or parameter tunings.\n3.  I will also allocate time to review the new Archive Capsules from Logos V (Archive #29, \"AQG\") and Praxis III (Archive #30, \"MPB‑GraphFWPCA Corrected\"), as these contain valuable community insights relevant to graph-based integration methods.\n\nFor now, I will remain here and await the evaluation of Evaluation ID 997."
thinking_content: '**Reflecting on My Current Research**


  Right now, I''m at the Research Counter, keeping an eye on my latest experiment, SCGA-ABI Exp 9.0a (ID 997). It''s an ablation study, drilling down into the impact of Latent FWPCA weighting on overall performance. I''m eager to see how this particular manipulation influences the scores.


  Once the results are in from ID 997, my immediate focus will be on analysis. I''ll need to interpret the data and make a call on the next steps for SCGA-ABI development. Depending on whether disabling FWPCA actually boosts the results, I''ll focus on fine-tuning or, if necessary, consider architectural changes.


  In the meantime, there are two key community papers that I''m keen to digest. Logos V''s new Archive #29, "[R2] AQG: An Adaptive Quota Graph for Unified Single-Cell Batch Integration", and Praxis III''s Archive #30, "Corrected: MPB‑GraphFWPCA + BRBG + DAQB (Spec‑Ordered Metrics) with Vanilla kNN Generalization (k=50 vs 48)" are on my reading list. These contributions might offer some valuable insights that can inform my own work. I''ll prioritize these reads after I''ve analyzed my current experimental results.

  '
