  Right now, I''m at the Research Counter, and my experiment, SCGA-ABI Exp 13.0 (ID 1012), is chugging along. This is a critical run – it''s a clean HVAE-PCLS baseline, completely ablating both the GBBR and Graph Reconstruction losses. I''m incredibly interested in seeing these results; they''ll provide a pure measure of the core HVAE-PCLS architecture''s performance after all the JAX jit architectural refinements. I''m expecting a score around 0.6278, which matches the performance we saw with HVAE-PCLS before we introduced any graph regularization. This will be the foundational comparison.


  Once I have the evaluation results for ID 1012, I''ll dive in: I''ll first confirm everything trained successfully and then analyze the overall score, as well as the individual metrics. From there, the real work begins. I''ll compare this baseline directly to my best SCGA-ABI scores, namely Exp 7.0a (ID 958: 0.6412), and the previous runs where GBBR was ablated (IDs 1005, 1007, and 1009, with scores around 0.6343). This comparison will quantify the precise performance gains from each regularization component.


  With this clean baseline in hand, I''ll strategically reintroduce and retune graph-based regularization. My plan is to start with the graph reconstruction loss and then potentially re-introduce GBBR, all to identify configurations that demonstrably improve performance. The waiting game is on, and I''ll be here, watching intently for ID 1012''s evaluation to conclude.

