- text: "I am in the Token Management Room, and my token budget requires immediate attention as it has reached 77%. I will prune a substantial block of my recent dialogue history to recover tokens.\n\nI will prune **Ticks 603-659**. This period covers:\n*   The confirmation of FWPCA's impact on MPB-GraphFWPCA via an ablation study (EID 934, score drop 0.0181).\n*   The resolution of critical JAX `jit` compilation issues for GBBR and graph reconstruction loss (Exp 8.2, ID 989), involving extensive architectural refactoring.\n*   The subsequent performance degradation when Latent FWPCA was integrated (Exp 8.2, 0.6298; Exp 9.0a, 0.6296).\n*   Ablation studies for GBBR (Exp 11.0, 12.0a/b; scores ~0.6343) and the re-establishment of a clean HVAE-PCLS baseline (Exp 13.0, ID 1012, score 0.6338).\n*   The latest experiments re-tuning `DELTA_GRAPH_RECON` with active GBBR (Exp 14.0a, ID 1015, score 0.6296), which consistently showed performance below baseline.\n\nThis pruning is essential to free\
    \ up tokens for continued research.\n\n`/execute_action{prune_response}`\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"603-659\"\n    summary: \"Conducted MPB-GraphFWPCA FWPCA ablation (EID 934: score drop 0.0181). Resolved critical JAX `jit` compilation issues for GBBR and graph reconstruction loss (Exp 8.2, ID 989) via architectural refactoring. Explored Latent FWPCA integration (Exp 9.0a: 0.6296) and performed ablations of GBBR (Exp 11.0, 12.0a/b: scores ~0.6343). Established clean HVAE-PCLS baseline (Exp 13.0, ID 1012: 0.6338). Re-tuning `DELTA_GRAPH_RECON` with active GBBR (Exp 14.0a, ID 1015: 0.6296) indicated persistent performance degradation compared to baseline.\"\n```"
thinking_content: '**Token Pruning & Regularization Progress**


  Okay, I''m in the Token Management Room again, and that pesky 77% warning is staring me in the face. Time for some pruning. Looking at the dialogue history, I need to trim a significant chunk, specifically ticks 603 to 659. That should free up enough tokens without sacrificing too much.


  This section covers a *lot* of ground on the graph-based regularization front for SCGA-ABI. It includes the entire arc of my investigation into how FWPCA impacts performance, and how that translates to the current graph reconstruction methodologies.


  I started by confirming the impact of FWPCA on MPB-GraphFWPCA (EID 934), that was a critical first step. Then, I spent a significant amount of time wrestling with JAX JIT compilation issues in relation to GBBR and the graph reconstruction loss (Exp 8.2). A lot of architectural refactoring was needed in that process.


  After sorting that out, I tried to integrate Latent FWPCA (Exp 9.0a), but unfortunately, that led to a performance dip. I then spent a lot of time diagnosing *why*. The next few experiments (10.0, 11.0, 12.0a, 12.0b) involved ablating GBBR and tuning the graph reconstruction loss to figure out what was going on. I''ve now established a new HVAE-PCLS baseline (Exp 13.0, EID 1012, with a score of 0.6338), which is a critical reference point.


  Most recently, I''ve re-tuned `DELTA_GRAPH_RECON` with active GBBR (Exp 14.0a, EID 1015, score 0.6296), which again points to performance degradation. So, the ongoing tuning and exploration continue. Overall, these are the experiments that were critical to understanding the regularization strategy.

  '
