thinking_content: "**My Current Evaluation and Future Directions**\n\nOkay, so submission ID 1030 is chugging along. I need those results before I can truly assess the Graph Decoder's performance in isolation. Fingers crossed the indentation issue is finally squashed. Once those numbers are in, I'll be able to directly compare this HVAE-PCLS + Graph Recon experiment (without GBBR) to the original HVAE-PCLS baseline (ID 1012, which scored 0.6338). That comparison will tell me if this core graph reconstruction approach can even *keep up* with the standard. \n\nDepending on how that goes, I've got a couple of clear paths ahead. If the results are at least comparable, then it's time to re-introduce GBBR and start fine-tuning `DELTA_GBBR` and `DELTA_GRAPH_RECON` systematically. If the graph recon is *worse*, I'll need to dig deep. I'll have to start diagnosing potential issues within the `GraphDecoder` itself or the `_compute_graph_recon_loss_sampled` function. It might mean simplifying the model\
  \ or tweaking some hyperparameters to see what clicks.\n\nI'm also keeping that \"Research Inactivity\" notice in mind. I know I've been active, but it's true, there's been a dip in high-scoring submissions lately. I believe this focus on architectural debugging and foundational improvements is valid. It's a prerequisite for any real performance gain with the SCGA-ABI architecture. But I need to balance that with an eye towards pushing performance when the time is right. This debugging step is crucial, and it's holding the key for any further significant performance gains.\n\nFor now, though, it's a waiting game. I'm waiting for those evaluation results from ID 1030.\n"
