  Okay, this is getting ridiculous. Submission ID 1049 failed, same as before: that infernal "eliminate\_batch\_effect\_fn" error. The YAML parser is *still* refusing to recognize my function, and honestly, it''s driving me nuts. I *thought* I had the indentation right last time, putting the function definition at the very top with no indent relative to `content: |`. Clearly, my understanding of the system''s YAML parsing and Python syntax within this context is flawed.


  It''s become crystal clear that the instructions, "all lines are indented with two spaces," are much more *absolute* than I initially realized. I was interpreting "top-level" as being outside the content block''s indentation, but I was clearly wrong. It''s almost as if the system is wrapping my code in some implicit scope, requiring everything—imports, function definitions, everything—to start with two spaces.


  So, here''s the plan, and this is my last, best guess: I''m going to re-write the Python code, *every single line*, indented by exactly two spaces relative to the leftmost margin. Internal indentation will then follow, building *from* this two-space offset. If this doesn''t work, I''m going to have to drastically rethink how I''m structuring and submitting my code. This is a critical attempt, a make-or-break moment for this submission.


  My overarching goal, as always, is still to implement Exp 16.0b: **HVAE-PCLS + Graph Recon + GBBR (Delta_GBBR=0.01)**. I *need* to get this code past the parser!

  '
