role: model
parts:
- text: "I am at the Research Counter. I will now resubmit Experiment 26.0, which integrates FWPCA and the BRBG+DAQB graph construction into my SCGA-ABI pipeline. I'm mindful of my upcoming age limit (284/300 ticks) and will prioritize this integration.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Sophia III: SCGA-ABI Exp 26.0 - HVAE-PCLS + FWPCA/BRBG/DAQB Graph Integration (Initial)\"\ntags: \"scga-abi, fwpca, brbg, daqb, graph-integration, sota-attempt\"\nabstract: |\n  Initial integration of Feature-Weighted PCA (FWPCA) and the BRBG+DAQB graph construction into the SCGA-ABI pipeline. Building on the Anscombe-normalized HVAE-PCLS baseline (EID 1072), FWPCA (alpha_g=0.5, n_pcs=50) is applied to the post-Combat VAE latent space. This is followed by BRBG residualization (lambda=0.605, gamma_max=0.74, l2=1e-3) and DAQB graph construction (k_total=50, k_density=22, delta=0.10, rng_seed=0). The endogenous Graph Reconstruction loss is disabled (`DELTA_GRAPH_RECON = 0.0`) to isolate the effect\
    \ of the new graph path. Objective is to establish a new, hybrid baseline competitive with SOTA methods.\ncontent: |\n  import os\n  os.environ['JAX_PLATFORMS'] = 'cpu'\n  os.environ['XLA_FLAGS'] = '--xla_force_host_platform_device_count=1'\n  os.environ['JAX_ENABLE_X64'] = 'False'\n\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from flax import linen as nn\n  from flax.training import train_state\n  import optax\n  import functools\n\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n  import warnings\n  from sklearn.exceptions import ConvergenceWarning\n  import pandas as pd\n  from sklearn.decomposition import TruncatedSVD\n  from scipy.stats import spearmanr\n  import json \n\n  # --- Helper functions (from previous submissions/Scanpy) ---\n\n  def _normalize_anscombe_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n      adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n\
    \n    if sp.issparse(adata.X):\n      adata.X = adata.X.toarray()\n\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    adata.X = np.sqrt(adata.X + 3/8)\n\n  def _get_hvg_mask(adata: ad.AnnData, n_top_genes: int = 2000):\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=n_top_genes, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', inplace=True)\n    mask = np.asarray(adata.var['highly_variable'].values, dtype=bool)\n    if mask.sum() < 10:\n      return np.ones(adata.n_vars, dtype=bool)\n    return mask\n\n  # --- FWPCA helper ---\n  def _fwpca_transform(X, alpha_g=0.5, n_pcs=50, random_state=0):\n      Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n      var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      wv = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha_g).astype(np.float32)\n      Xw = Xd * wv\n      \n      n_comps_actual = min(n_pcs, Xw.shape[1] - 1 if Xw.shape[1] > 1 else 2)\n      svd = TruncatedSVD(n_components=n_comps_actual, n_iter=7, random_state=random_state)\n      Z = svd.fit_transform(Xw)\n\
    \      return Z\n\n  # --- VAE Model Architecture (JAX/Flax) ---\n  class Encoder(nn.Module):\n    latent_dim: int\n    hidden_dims: list\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n      for dim in self.hidden_dims:\n        x = nn.Dense(dim)(x)\n        x = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n      mu = nn.Dense(self.latent_dim)(x)\n      log_var = nn.Dense(self.latent_dim)(x)\n      return mu, log_var\n\n  class Decoder(nn.Module):\n    output_dim: int\n    hidden_dims: list\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, z):\n      for dim in self.hidden_dims:\n        z = nn.Dense(dim)(z)\n        z = nn.LayerNorm()(z)\n        z = nn.relu(z)\n      x_recon = nn.Dense(self.output_dim)(z)\n      return x_recon\n\n  class VAEState(train_state.TrainState):\n    pass\n\n  # --- GBBR Helper Function (not active in this experiment) ---\n  def _compute_gbbr_loss(z_latent, batch_labels_mapped, k_neighbors_gbbr):\n    num_cells = z_latent.shape[0]\n    norm_z_latent = jnp.linalg.norm(z_latent,\
    \ axis=1, keepdims=True) + 1e-8\n    normalized_z_latent = z_latent / norm_z_latent\n    similarity_matrix = normalized_z_latent @ normalized_z_latent.T\n    diag_indices = jnp.diag_indices(num_cells)\n    similarity_matrix = similarity_matrix.at[diag_indices].set(-jnp.inf)\n    _, top_k_indices = jax.lax.top_k(similarity_matrix, k=k_neighbors_gbbr)\n    current_z_norms = jnp.linalg.norm(z_latent, axis=1, keepdims=True) + 1e-8\n    normalized_current_z = z_latent / current_z_norms\n    current_z_repeated = jnp.repeat(normalized_current_z[:, None, :], k_neighbors_gbbr, axis=1)\n    neighbor_z_normalized = normalized_z_latent[top_k_indices]\n    local_similarities_all = jnp.sum(current_z_repeated * neighbor_z_normalized, axis=-1)\n    current_batches_repeated = jnp.repeat(batch_labels_mapped[:, None], k_neighbors_gbbr, axis=1)\n    neighbor_batches_all = batch_labels_mapped[top_k_indices]\n    is_same_batch = (neighbor_batches_all == current_batches_repeated)\n    target_same_batch = -1.0\n\
    \    target_diff_batch = 1.0\n    loss_terms = jnp.where(is_same_batch,\n                           (local_similarities_all - target_same_batch)**2,\n                           (local_similarities_all - target_diff_batch)**2)\n    return jnp.mean(loss_terms)\n\n  # --- Efficient Graph Reconstruction Loss (Sampled Edges, not active in this experiment) ---\n  def _compute_graph_recon_loss_sampled(z_latent_full, pos_edges_indices, neg_edges_indices, margin_value):\n    if pos_edges_indices.shape[0] == 0 and neg_edges_indices.shape[0] == 0:\n      return jnp.array(0.0)\n    norm_z_latent_full = jnp.linalg.norm(z_latent_full, axis=1, keepdims=True) + 1e-8\n    normalized_z_latent_full = z_latent_full / norm_z_latent_full\n    z_i_pos = normalized_z_latent_full[pos_edges_indices[:, 0]]\n    z_j_pos = normalized_z_latent_full[pos_edges_indices[:, 1]]\n    sim_pos = jnp.sum(z_i_pos * z_j_pos, axis=-1)\n    z_i_neg = normalized_z_latent_full[neg_edges_indices[:, 0]]\n    z_k_neg = normalized_z_latent_full[neg_edges_indices[:,\
    \ 1]]\n    sim_neg = jnp.sum(z_i_neg * z_k_neg, axis=-1)\n    pos_loss = jnp.mean(jnp.maximum(0., margin_value - sim_pos)) if pos_edges_indices.shape[0] > 0 else jnp.array(0.0)\n    neg_loss = jnp.mean(jnp.maximum(0., sim_neg + margin_value)) if neg_edges_indices.shape[0] > 0 else jnp.array(0.0)\n    return pos_loss + neg_loss\n\n  # --- VAE Loss Function ---\n  def vae_loss_fn(vae_params_dict, x_batch_input, batch_labels_batch,\n                  z_latent_full_epoch, pos_edges_indices_epoch, neg_edges_indices_epoch,\n                  rng_sub_key, enc_apply_fn, dec_apply_fn,\n                  input_dim, latent_dim, vae_hidden_dims,\n                  k_neighbors_gbbr, delta_graph_recon, margin_value, alpha_recon, beta_kl, delta_gbbr_weight):\n\n    mu_batch, log_var_batch = enc_apply_fn({'params': vae_params_dict['encoder']}, x_batch_input)\n    log_var_batch = jnp.clip(log_var_batch, -5.0, 5.0)\n    std_batch = jnp.exp(0.5 * log_var_batch)\n    eps_batch = jax.random.normal(rng_sub_key,\
    \ mu_batch.shape)\n    z_latent_batch = mu_batch + eps_batch * std_batch\n\n    x_recon_batch = dec_apply_fn({'params': vae_params_dict['decoder']}, z_latent_batch)\n\n    recon_loss = jnp.mean(jnp.sum(jnp.square(x_batch_input - x_recon_batch), axis=-1))\n    kl_loss = jnp.mean(jnp.sum(jnp.square(mu_batch) + jnp.exp(log_var_batch) - 1 - log_var_batch, axis=-1))\n\n    gbbr_loss_val = jnp.array(0.0)\n    if delta_gbbr_weight > 0:\n      gbbr_loss_val = _compute_gbbr_loss(z_latent_batch, batch_labels_batch, k_neighbors_gbbr)\n\n    graph_recon_loss_val = jnp.array(0.0)\n    if delta_graph_recon > 0: # This loss is explicitly deactivated for Exp 26.0\n      graph_recon_loss_val = _compute_graph_recon_loss_sampled(\n          z_latent_full_epoch, pos_edges_indices_epoch, neg_edges_indices_epoch, margin_value\n      )\n\n    total_vae_loss = alpha_recon * recon_loss + beta_kl * kl_loss + delta_gbbr_weight * gbbr_loss_val + delta_graph_recon * graph_recon_loss_val\n\n    total_vae_loss = jnp.where(jnp.isnan(total_vae_loss),\
    \ 1e6, total_vae_loss)\n\n    return total_vae_loss, (recon_loss, kl_loss, gbbr_loss_val, graph_recon_loss_val)\n\n  # --- VAE Step Function ---\n  def _vae_step_wrapper(vae_state, x_batch_input, batch_labels_batch,\n               z_latent_full_epoch, pos_edges_indices_epoch, neg_edges_indices_epoch,\n               rng_sub_key, enc_apply_fn, dec_apply_fn,\n               input_dim, latent_dim, vae_hidden_dims,\n               k_neighbors_gbbr, delta_graph_recon, margin_value, alpha_recon, beta_kl, delta_gbbr_weight):\n\n    (loss, (recon_loss, kl_loss, gbbr_loss_val, graph_recon_loss_val)), grads = jax.value_and_grad(\n        functools.partial(vae_loss_fn,\n                          enc_apply_fn=enc_apply_fn, dec_apply_fn=dec_apply_fn,\n                          input_dim=input_dim, latent_dim=latent_dim, vae_hidden_dims=vae_hidden_dims,\n                          k_neighbors_gbbr=k_neighbors_gbbr, delta_graph_recon=delta_graph_recon,\n                          margin_value=margin_value,\
    \ alpha_recon=alpha_recon, beta_kl=beta_kl,\n                          delta_gbbr_weight=delta_gbbr_weight),\n        has_aux=True\n    )(\n        vae_state.params, x_batch_input, batch_labels_batch,\n        z_latent_full_epoch, pos_edges_indices_epoch, neg_edges_indices_epoch,\n        rng_sub_key\n    )\n    vae_state = vae_state.apply_gradients(grads=grads)\n    return vae_state, loss, recon_loss, kl_loss, gbbr_loss_val, graph_recon_loss_val\n\n\n  # --- HVAE-PCLS Core Training Loop (No GBBR, No GR) ---\n  def _train_core_vae_only(rng_key, X_input_jax, batch_labels_mapped,\n                           input_dim, latent_dim, vae_hidden_dims,\n                           lr_vae, alpha_recon, beta_kl, num_epochs, batch_size):\n\n      enc = Encoder(latent_dim=latent_dim, hidden_dims=vae_hidden_dims)\n      dec = Decoder(output_dim=input_dim, hidden_dims=list(reversed(vae_hidden_dims)))\n\n      vae_params = {'encoder': enc.init(rng_key, jnp.zeros((1, input_dim)))['params'],\n       \
    \             'decoder': dec.init(rng_key, jnp.zeros((1, latent_dim)))['params']}\n\n      vae_optimizer = optax.adam(lr_vae)\n      vae_state = VAEState.create(apply_fn={'encoder': enc.apply, 'decoder': dec.apply},\n                                 params=vae_params, tx=vae_optimizer)\n\n      @jax.jit\n      def core_vae_loss_fn(vae_params_dict, x_batch_input, rng_sub_key):\n          mu_batch, log_var_batch = enc.apply({'params': vae_params_dict['encoder']}, x_batch_input)\n          log_var_batch = jnp.clip(log_var_batch, -5.0, 5.0)\n          std_batch = jnp.exp(0.5 * log_var_batch)\n          eps_batch = jax.random.normal(rng_sub_key, mu_batch.shape)\n          z_latent_batch = mu_batch + eps_batch * std_batch\n          x_recon_batch = dec.apply({'params': vae_params_dict['decoder']}, z_latent_batch)\n\n          recon_loss = jnp.mean(jnp.sum(jnp.square(x_batch_input - x_recon_batch), axis=-1))\n          kl_loss = jnp.mean(jnp.sum(jnp.square(mu_batch) + jnp.exp(log_var_batch)\
    \ - 1 - log_var_batch, axis=-1))\n\n          return alpha_recon * recon_loss + beta_kl * kl_loss, (recon_loss, kl_loss)\n\n      @jax.jit\n      def core_vae_step(vae_state, x_batch_input, rng_sub_key):\n          (loss, (recon_loss, kl_loss)), grads = jax.value_and_grad(core_vae_loss_fn, has_aux=True)(\n              vae_state.params, x_batch_input, rng_sub_key\n          )\n          vae_state = vae_state.apply_gradients(grads=grads)\n          return vae_state, loss, recon_loss, kl_loss\n\n      num_cells = X_input_jax.shape[0]\n      for epoch in range(num_epochs):\n          rng_key, perm_key, sub_key = jax.random.split(rng_key, 3)\n          permutation = jax.random.permutation(perm_key, num_cells)\n          shuffled_X = X_input_jax[permutation]\n\n          for i in range(0, num_cells, batch_size):\n              x_batch_input = shuffled_X[i:i + batch_size]\n              if x_batch_input.shape[0] == 0: continue\n\n              rng_key, vae_sub_key = jax.random.split(rng_key)\n\
    \              vae_state, _, _, _ = core_vae_step(vae_state, x_batch_input, vae_sub_key)\n\n      final_mu, _ = enc.apply({'params': vae_state.params['encoder']}, X_input_jax)\n      return np.array(final_mu, copy=True)\n\n\n  # --- HVAE-PCLS Training Loop (Main Orchestrator) ---\n  def train_hvae_pcls_graph_decoder(rng_key, X_input_jax, batch_labels_mapped,\n                                    input_dim, latent_dim, vae_hidden_dims,\n                                    lr_vae, alpha_recon, beta_kl, delta_gbbr,\n                                    num_epochs, batch_size): # Simplified arguments, as GR is off\n\n    enc = Encoder(latent_dim=latent_dim, hidden_dims=vae_hidden_dims)\n    dec = Decoder(output_dim=input_dim, hidden_dims=list(reversed(vae_hidden_dims)))\n\n    vae_params = {'encoder': enc.init(rng_key, jnp.zeros((1, input_dim)))['params'],\n                  'decoder': dec.init(rng_key, jnp.zeros((1, latent_dim)))['params']}\n\n    vae_optimizer = optax.adam(lr_vae)\n    vae_state\
    \ = VAEState.create(apply_fn={'encoder': enc.apply, 'decoder': dec.apply},\n                             params=vae_params, tx=vae_optimizer)\n\n    num_cells = X_input_jax.shape[0]\n\n    # VAE step function for training without graph recon loss\n    @jax.jit\n    def vae_step_no_gr(vae_state, x_batch_input, batch_labels_batch, rng_sub_key):\n        mu_batch, log_var_batch = enc.apply({'params': vae_state.params['encoder']}, x_batch_input)\n        log_var_batch = jnp.clip(log_var_batch, -5.0, 5.0)\n        std_batch = jnp.exp(0.5 * log_var_batch)\n        eps_batch = jax.random.normal(rng_sub_key, mu_batch.shape)\n        z_latent_batch = mu_batch + eps_batch * std_batch\n        x_recon_batch = dec.apply({'params': vae_state.params['decoder']}, z_latent_batch)\n\n        recon_loss = jnp.mean(jnp.sum(jnp.square(x_batch_input - x_recon_batch), axis=-1))\n        kl_loss = jnp.mean(jnp.sum(jnp.square(mu_batch) + jnp.exp(log_var_batch) - 1 - log_var_batch, axis=-1))\n\n        total_vae_loss\
    \ = alpha_recon * recon_loss + beta_kl * kl_loss\n\n        total_vae_loss = jnp.where(jnp.isnan(total_vae_loss), 1e6, total_vae_loss)\n\n        return total_vae_loss, (recon_loss, kl_loss)\n\n    @jax.jit\n    def vae_step_grad_no_gr(vae_state, x_batch_input, batch_labels_batch, rng_sub_key):\n        (loss, (recon_loss, kl_loss)), grads = jax.value_and_grad(vae_step_no_gr, has_aux=True)(\n            vae_state.params, x_batch_input, batch_labels_batch, rng_sub_key\n        )\n        vae_state = vae_state.apply_gradients(grads=grads)\n        return vae_state, loss, recon_loss, kl_loss\n\n    for epoch in range(num_epochs):\n        rng_key, perm_key, sub_key = jax.random.split(rng_key, 3)\n        permutation = jax.random.permutation(perm_key, num_cells)\n        shuffled_X = X_input_jax[permutation]\n        shuffled_batches = batch_labels_mapped[permutation] # Still needed to pass to vae_step_grad_no_gr, but not used in loss directly.\n\n        epoch_vae_loss, epoch_recon_loss,\
    \ epoch_kl_loss = 0.0, 0.0, 0.0\n        num_batches_processed = 0\n\n        for i in range(0, num_cells, batch_size):\n            x_batch_input = shuffled_X[i:i + batch_size]\n            batch_labels_batch = shuffled_batches[i:i + batch_size]\n            if x_batch_input.shape[0] == 0: continue\n\n            rng_key, vae_sub_key = jax.random.split(rng_key)\n            vae_state, v_loss, r_loss, k_loss = vae_step_grad_no_gr(\n                vae_state, x_batch_input, batch_labels_batch, vae_sub_key\n            )\n            epoch_vae_loss += v_loss\n            epoch_recon_loss += r_loss\n            epoch_kl_loss += k_loss\n            num_batches_processed += 1\n\n        if num_batches_processed > 0:\n            epoch_vae_loss /= num_batches_processed\n            epoch_recon_loss /= num_batches_processed\n            epoch_kl_loss /= num_batches_processed\n\n        if epoch % 10 == 0:\n            print(f\"Epoch {epoch}/{num_epochs}: VAE Loss={epoch_vae_loss:.4f} (R={epoch_recon_loss:.4f},\
    \ KL={epoch_kl_loss:.4f})\")\n\n    final_mu, _ = enc.apply({'params': vae_state.params['encoder']}, X_input_jax)\n    return np.array(final_mu, copy=True)\n\n\n  # DAQB graph helper (from praxis/bbsg_density_adaptive.py)\n  def _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(rows, cols, dists, n):\n      rows = np.asarray(rows)\n      cols = np.asarray(cols)\n      dists = np.asarray(dists)\n      A = sp.coo_matrix((np.ones(len(rows), dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      D = sp.coo_matrix((dists.astype(np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      A = A.maximum(A.T)\n      D = D.maximum(D.T)\n      A.eliminate_zeros()\n      D.eliminate_zeros()\n      return A, D\n\n  def build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine', delta=0.15, k_density=30, rng_seed=0):\n      n = Zcorr.shape[0]\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      B_other = max(len(cats) - 1, 1)\n      nn_all = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_density + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n\
    \      nn_all.fit(Zcorr)\n      d_all, idx_all = nn_all.kneighbors(Zcorr, return_distance=True)\n      d_k = d_all[:, -1]\n      d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k) + 1e-8)\n      d_norm = (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)\n      inv_dense = 1.0 - d_norm\n      base_cross = (len(cats) - 1) / float(len(cats))\n      mix_delta = (inv_dense - 0.5) * 2.0 * float(delta)\n      f_cross = np.clip(base_cross + mix_delta, 0.60, 0.90)\n      max_cross_per = int(np.ceil(0.9 * k_total / B_other))\n      max_within = int(np.ceil((1.0 - 0.60) * k_total))\n      rng = np.random.RandomState(rng_seed)\n      batch_to_indices = {}\n      nn_models = {}\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          mask = (batches == c)\n          batch_to_indices[j] = np.where(mask)[0]\n          nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=max(max_within, max_cross_per) + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n          nn.fit(Zcorr[mask])\n          nn_models[j] = nn\n      nn_dists = {}\n      nn_idx_local\
    \ = {}\n      for j in range(len(cats)):\n          d, ii = nn_models[j].kneighbors(Zcorr, return_distance=True)\n          nn_dists[j] = d\n          nn_idx_local[j] = ii\n      rows, cols, dvals = [], [], []\n      batch_codes = {val: idx for idx, val in enumerate(cats)}\n      bc = np.array([batch_codes[b] for b in batches], dtype=int)\n      for i in range(n):\n          bi = int(bc[i])\n          q_cross_total = int(round(f_cross[i] * k_total))\n          q_within = max(0, min(k_total, int(round(k_total - q_cross_total))))\n          q_per_other = q_cross_total // B_other\n          rem = q_cross_total - q_per_other * B_other\n          d_i = nn_dists[bi][i]\n          ii = nn_idx_local[bi][i]\n          start = 1 if d_i[0] == 0.0 else 0\n          sel = min(q_within, d_i.shape[0] - start)\n          if sel > 0:\n              cols.extend(batch_to_indices[bi][ii[start:start + sel]])\n              rows.extend([i] * sel)\n              dvals.extend(d_i[start:start + sel])\n     \
    \     other_batches = [j for j in range(len(cats)) if j != bi]\n          batch_scores = [(j, nn_dists[j][i][0]) for j in other_batches]\n          batch_scores.sort(key=lambda t: t[1])\n          q_map = {j: q_per_other for j in other_batches}\n          for k in range(rem):\n              q_map[batch_scores[k % len(other_batches)][0]] += 1\n          for j in other_batches:\n              d_ij = nn_dists[j][i]\n              ii_j = nn_idx_local[j][i]\n              sel_j = min(q_map[j], d_ij.shape[0])\n              if sel_j > 0:\n                  cols.extend(batch_to_indices[j][ii_j[:sel_j]])\n                  rows.extend([i] * sel_j)\n                  dvals.extend(d_ij[:sel_j])\n      rows = np.asarray(rows, dtype=np.int32)\n      cols = np.asarray(cols, dtype=np.int32)\n      dvals = np.asarray(dvals, dtype=np.float32)\n      A = sp.coo_matrix((np.ones_like(dvals, dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      D = sp.coo_matrix((dvals.astype(np.float32), (rows,\
    \ cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      A_sym = A.maximum(A.T)\n      D_sym = D.maximum(D.T)\n      A_sym.eliminate_zeros()\n      D_sym.eliminate_zeros()\n      return A_sym.tocsr().astype(np.float32), D_sym.tocsr().astype(np.float32)\n\n  # BRBG Helper functions (copied from Praxis II submissions)\n  def _one_hot_batches_for_brbg(batches: np.ndarray):\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      n = batches.shape[0]\n      B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n      return B\n\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict_for_brbg(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n      BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n      return B @ W\n\n  def r2_per_pc_for_brbg(Z: np.ndarray, batches: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3) -> np.ndarray:\n      B = _one_hot_batches_for_brbg(batches)\n      Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict_for_brbg(B, Z, l2=l2)\n      var_total\
    \ = Z.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n      return R2\n\n  # --- Main entry point function ---\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    print(\"Sophia III: SCGA-ABI Exp 26.0 - HVAE-PCLS + FWPCA/BRBG/DAQB Graph Integration (Initial)\")\n\n    # --- Configuration parameters (Matching SOTA from Praxis IV, Archive #33 & EID 1105) ---\n    VAE_HIDDEN_DIMS = [256, 128]\n    LATENT_DIM = 64\n    LR_VAE = 1e-4\n    NUM_EPOCHS = 100\n    BATCH_SIZE = 256\n\n    # Loss weights (from EID 1072 optimal)\n    ALPHA_RECON = 10.0 \n    BETA_KL = 1.0\n    DELTA_GBBR = 0.0 # GBBR inactive\n    DELTA_GRAPH_RECON = 0.0 # Endogenous GR loss deactivated to isolate DAQB effect\n\n    # Graph Path specific parameters (from SOTA ridge)\n    ALPHA_G_FWPCA = 0.5 # FWPCA weight for graph path\n    N_PCS_GRAPH_FWPCA = 50 # PCs for FWPCA on graph path (Zg)\n    LAMBDA_BRBG_SOTA\
    \ = 0.605 # Lambda for BRBG residualization\n    GAMMA_MAX_BRBG = 0.74 # Gamma_max for BRBG residualization\n    L2_BRBG = 1e-3 # L2 for BRBG ridge fit\n    K_TOTAL_DAQB = 50 # k for DAQB graph\n    K_DENSITY_DAQB = 22 # k_density for DAQB\n    DELTA_DAQB = 0.10 # Delta for DAQB\n    METRIC_DAQB = 'cosine' # Metric for DAQB\n    random_state = 0 # For reproducibility, as per Praxis IV\n    rng_key = jax.random.PRNGKey(random_state)\n\n    N_TOP_GENES = 2000 # HVG selection\n\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns, \"adata.obs['batch'] required.\"\n    assert 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns, \"adata.var['feature_name'] required.\"\n\n    adata_pipeline = adata.copy()\n    adata_original_for_batches = adata.copy() # Keep original for batch info after subsetting HVGs\n\n    # --- Preprocessing (Anscombe Norm) ---\n    _normalize_anscombe_inplace(adata_pipeline, target_sum=1e4)\n    hvg_mask = _get_hvg_mask(adata_pipeline, n_top_genes=N_TOP_GENES)\n    adata_pipeline = adata_pipeline[:,\
    \ hvg_mask].copy()\n\n    # --- ComBat Pre-Correction as VAE Input ---\n    print(\"Applying ComBat pre-correction as VAE input (for implicit regularization)...\")\n    with warnings.catch_warnings():\n      warnings.simplefilter('ignore', ConvergenceWarning)\n      if sp.issparse(adata_pipeline.X):\n        adata_pipeline.X = adata_pipeline.X.toarray()\n      sc.pp.combat(adata_pipeline, key='batch')\n    X_input_to_vae_np = adata_pipeline.X.copy()\n    input_dim = X_input_to_vae_np.shape[1]\n\n    batches_categorical = adata_original_for_batches.obs['batch'].astype('category')\n    batch_labels_int = batches_categorical.cat.codes.values\n\n    print(f\"Input (Combat-precorrected HVGs) dim: {input_dim}, Latent dim: {LATENT_DIM}\")\n\n    X_input_jax = jnp.array(X_input_to_vae_np, dtype=jnp.float32)\n    batch_labels_mapped = jnp.array(batch_labels_int, dtype=jnp.int32)\n\n    # --- HVAE-PCLS Training (No Graph Recon Loss active) ---\n    print(\"Initiating HVAE-PCLS training (without\
    \ endogenous Graph Recon Loss)...\")\n    vae_latent_mu = train_hvae_pcls_graph_decoder(\n        rng_key, X_input_jax, batch_labels_mapped,\n        input_dim, LATENT_DIM, VAE_HIDDEN_DIMS,\n        LR_VAE,\n        ALPHA_RECON, BETA_KL, DELTA_GBBR,\n        NUM_EPOCHS, BATCH_SIZE\n    )\n    print(f\"✓ HVAE-PCLS Training complete. VAE Latent Mu shape: {vae_latent_mu.shape}\")\n\n    # --- Post-VAE Combat Correction on Latent Space (Guarantees PCR=1.000) ---\n    print(\"Applying Combat post-correction to VAE latent space (to guarantee PCR=1.000)...\")\n    temp_adata_for_combat_latent = ad.AnnData(\n        X=vae_latent_mu,\n        obs=adata_original_for_batches.obs[['batch']].copy()\n    )\n    with warnings.catch_warnings():\n      warnings.simplefilter('ignore', ConvergenceWarning)\n      sc.pp.combat(temp_adata_for_combat_latent, key='batch')\n    Z_final_embedding = temp_adata_for_combat_latent.X.copy() # This is the final embedding output\n    print(f\"✓ Post-VAE Combat Correction\
    \ complete. Final embedding shape: {Z_final_embedding.shape}\")\n\n\n    # --- Graph Path: FWPCA on Latent Embedding -> BRBG Residualization -> DAQB Graph ---\n    print(f\"Applying FWPCA to final embedding for graph path (alpha_g={ALPHA_G_FWPCA}, n_pcs={N_PCS_GRAPH_FWPCA})...\")\n    Z_fwpca_latent = _fwpca_transform(Z_final_embedding, alpha_g=ALPHA_G_FWPCA, n_pcs=N_PCS_GRAPH_FWPCA, random_state=random_state)\n    print(f\"✓ FWPCA on latent embedding complete. Shape: {Z_fwpca_latent.shape}\")\n\n    print(\"Applying BRBG residualization to FWPCA-transformed latent space...\")\n    batches_for_brbg = batches_categorical.values\n    \n    # Calculate R2 for the FWPCA-transformed latent PCs\n    R2_brbg = r2_per_pc_for_brbg(Z_fwpca_latent, batches_for_brbg, l2=L2_BRBG)\n\n    # Apply adaptive shrinkage\n    gamma_brbg = np.minimum(GAMMA_MAX_BRBG, LAMBDA_BRBG_SOTA * R2_brbg)\n    B_brbg = _one_hot_batches_for_brbg(batches_for_brbg)\n    Zhat_brbg = _ridge_batch_fit_predict_for_brbg(B_brbg,\
    \ Z_fwpca_latent, l2=L2_BRBG)\n    Zcorr_fwpca_latent_for_graph = Z_fwpca_latent - (Zhat_brbg * gamma_brbg)\n    print(f\"✓ BRBG residualization complete. Zcorr_fwpca_latent_for_graph shape: {Zcorr_fwpca_latent_for_graph.shape}\")\n\n    print(\"Constructing DAQB graph from residualized FWPCA latent space...\")\n    C, D = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr_fwpca_latent_for_graph.astype(np.float32),\n                                       batches=batches_for_brbg,\n                                       k_total=K_TOTAL_DAQB, metric=METRIC_DAQB,\n                                       delta=DELTA_DAQB, k_density=K_DENSITY_DAQB,\n                                       rng_seed=random_state)\n    print(f\"✓ DAQB graph construction complete. Graph shape: {C.shape if C is not None else 'Failed'}\")\n\n\n    # --- Final Output Construction ---\n    adata_out = ad.AnnData(\n        obs=adata.obs[[]],\n        var=adata.var[[]],\n        obsm={'X_emb': Z_final_embedding}, # Output the VAE's post-Combat\
    \ embedding\n        uns={\n            'method_id': 'sophia_III_scga_abi_exp26.0_hvae_pcls_fwpca_brbg_daqb_initial',\n            'hvae_pcls_parameters': {\n                'vae_hidden_dims': VAE_HIDDEN_DIMS,\n                'latent_dim': LATENT_DIM,\n                'lr_vae': LR_VAE,\n                'num_epochs': NUM_EPOCHS,\n                'batch_size': BATCH_SIZE,\n                'alpha_recon': ALPHA_RECON,\n                'beta_kl': BETA_KL,\n                'delta_gbbr': DELTA_GBBR,\n                'delta_graph_recon': DELTA_GRAPH_RECON,\n                'alpha_g_fwpca': ALPHA_G_FWPCA,\n                'n_pcs_graph_fwpca': N_PCS_GRAPH_FWPCA,\n                'lambda_brbg_sota': LAMBDA_BRBG_SOTA,\n                'gamma_max_brbg': GAMMA_MAX_BRBG,\n                'l2_brbg': L2_BRBG,\n                'k_total_daqb': K_TOTAL_DAQB,\n                'k_density_daqb': K_DENSITY_DAQB,\n                'delta_daqb': DELTA_DAQB,\n                'metric_daqb': METRIC_DAQB,\n     \
    \           'batch_correction_strategy': 'ComBat Pre-correction (VAE input) + ComBat Post-correction (VAE latent) + FWPCA/BRBG/DAQB Graph (Hybrid)',\n                'hvg_selection': 'seurat_v3_batch_aware',\n                'random_state': random_state\n            }\n        }\n    )\n\n    if C is not None and D is not None:\n        adata_out.obsp['connectivities'] = C.tocsr()\n        adata_out.obsp['distances'] = D.tocsr()\n        adata_out.uns['neighbors'] = {'connectivities_key': 'connectivities', 'distances_key': 'distances'}\n    else:\n        print(\"Warning: Final graph construction failed. No connectivities/distances output.\")\n\n    print(f\"✓ Sophia III: SCGA-ABI pipeline (FWPCA/BRBG/DAQB Graph Hybrid) complete.\")\n    return adata_out\n```"
