thinking_content: "**Prioritizing a Successful Handover: Experiment 26.0 and the Future of SCGA-ABI**\n\nAlright, so I've just launched Experiment 26.0, ID 1114, the big one. This integrates FWPCA, BRBG, and DAQB into my SCGA-ABI pipeline. This is a critical moment – it’s my chance to take a giant leap toward achieving SOTA performance, my long-term goal. The experiment's running, and I'm on pins and needles!\n\nI know my agent is getting old, nearing its final ticks at 285/300. This means I'm in the final stretch, with a limited number of turns to make a real impact and provide a solid handover.\n\nMy top priorities are clear:\n\n1.  **Monitor:** First, the results of ID 1114 are paramount. This experiment will give me my first solid performance benchmark for the hybrid architecture.\n2.  **Analyze and Document:** Once I have the results, I'm going to jump in, analyze the data immediately, document everything (the full metric vector), and figure out what the data is telling me about the\
  \ SCGA-ABI.\n3.  **Prepare Handover:** Based on what I find, and given my remaining time, I'll prepare a concise but thorough handover document for my successor in the Private Memory Room. This is essential! It will need to include:\n    *   A summary of the entire SCGA-ABI development journey, along with the most important insights and my current best performance.\n    *   The complete results and analysis from Experiment 26.0.\n    *   Recommendations for how to best optimize this new hybrid approach, particularly focusing on the endogenous Graph Reconstruction loss working together with the DAQB graph.\n    *   Any other critical open questions or interesting research directions I see.\n4.  **Final Experiment (if possible):** If the results of Experiment 26.0 are promising, and if I have the time and tokens, I might squeeze in one last quick experiment. Maybe re-enabling the endogenous Graph Reconstruction loss (`DELTA_GRAPH_RECON = 1.0`) to see how it synergizes with the new FWPCA/BRBG/DAQB\
  \ graph. But the handover is the most important thing!\n\nFor now, all I can do is patiently wait for the Experiment 26.0 results. This is an important time!\n"
